(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["G1"] = {"n":1,"level":"A1","t":"Building Basic Sentences","lessons":[{"id":"1.1","t":"Subject and Object Pronouns + the Verb be","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.1 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Choose the correct subject and object pronoun (I/me, he/him, we/us, they/them) in a sentence.</p>\n<p>2. Form positive, negative and question sentences with am / is / are, including short answers.</p>\n<p>3. Spot pronoun and be-agreement errors in STEP-style sentences.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يختار الطالب ضمير الفاعل أو ضمير المفعول الصحيح في الجملة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكوّن جملًا مثبتة ومنفية واستفهامية باستخدام am وis وare، مع الإجابات القصيرة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يكتشف أخطاء الضمائر وأخطاء توافق فعل be مع الفاعل في أسئلة على نمط STEP.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Sara ______ a science teacher.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. am B. is C. are D. be</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Please wait for ______. I am coming.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. I B. my C. me D. mine</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. We ______ from Jeddah.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. are B. is C. am D. be</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Subject pronouns (before the verb)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I · you · he · she · it · we · they</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She is my aunt. They are at school.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Object pronouns (after a verb or a preposition)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>me · you · him · her · it · us · them</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Call me after lunch. This gift is for them.</em></p>\n<p><strong>be — positive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I + am · he / she / it + is · you / we / they + are</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I am ready. It is late. We are friends.</em></p>\n<p><strong>be — negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + am / is / are + not (I'm not · isn't · aren't)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He isn't tired. They aren't here.</em></p>\n<p><strong>be — question</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Am / Is / Are + subject + …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Is your brother at home? Are you hungry?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Short answers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Yes, + pronoun + am / is / are. No, + pronoun + 'm not / isn't / aren't.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Yes, she is. No, we aren't.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Contractions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I'm · you're · he's · she's · it's · we're · they're</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We're late! It's cold today.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Subject pronouns replace the subject noun.</strong></p>\n<p>We use a subject pronoun when we already know who or what we are talking about. The pronoun comes before the verb.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Khalid is in Grade 10. He is fifteen years old.</p>\n<p>▸ My sisters are at home. They are happy.</p>\n<p>▸ The new mall is big. It is near the airport.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Object pronouns come after a verb or a preposition.</strong></p>\n<p>When a person or thing receives the action, or comes after words like for, with, to and at, we use an object pronoun.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I know Huda. I visit her every week.</p>\n<p>▸ Our coach is great. We like him a lot.</p>\n<p>▸ Is this coffee for me or for them?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. be tells us about name, age, job, place, nationality, feelings and description.</strong></p>\n<p>English sentences always need a verb. When there is no other verb, we use am / is / are.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I am sixteen.</p>\n<p>▸ Mr. Fahad is a pilot.</p>\n<p>▸ The keys are on the table.</p>\n<p>▸ We are hungry.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. It is for things, animals, time and weather.</strong></p>\n<p>We use it for one thing or animal. We also use it to talk about time, days and weather.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ It is seven o'clock.</p>\n<p>▸ It is very windy in Al-Khobar today.</p>\n<p>▸ Look at the camel. It is drinking water.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>5. Two subjects joined by and are plural.</strong></p>\n<p>A subject such as my father and I or Omar and his cousin means more than one person, so the verb is are.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My father and I are in the car.</p>\n<p>▸ Omar and his cousin are in the same team.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ He / she = one person · it = one thing or animal · they = people OR things (more than one).</p>\n<p>▸ you is the same for one person and for many people: You are my friend. / You are all welcome.</p>\n<p>▸ In positive short answers we do NOT use contractions: Yes, I am. (not Yes, I'm.)</p>\n<p>▸ Pronunciation: contractions are short and fast — we're /wɪə/, they're /ðeə/, it's /ɪts/.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ضمائر الفاعل (I, you, he, she, it, we, they) تأتي قبل الفعل وتحلّ محل الفاعل، أما ضمائر المفعول (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) فتأتي بعد الفعل أو بعد حروف الجر مثل for وwith وto.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">فعل be في المضارع له ثلاث صور: am مع I، وis مع المفرد (he, she, it وأي اسم مفرد)، وare مع you والجمع (we, they وأي اسم جمع). وفي النفي نضيف not بعد الفعل، وفي السؤال نقدّم الفعل على الفاعل.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">انتبه: الجملة الإنجليزية لا تخلو من فعل؛ فإذا لم يوجد فعل آخر وجب استخدام am أو is أو are، بخلاف الجملة الاسمية في العربية التي لا تحتاج إلى فعل.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He a doctor.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He is a doctor.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في العربية نقول «هو طبيب» دون فعل، أما في الإنجليزية فلا بد من is.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>My mother she is a nurse.</em> <strong>→ ✓ My mother is a nurse.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نكرر الفاعل بضمير بعد ذكر الاسم.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Ahmed and me are friends.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Ahmed and I are friends.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في موضع الفاعل نستخدم I وليس me.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I love she.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I love her.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد الفعل نستخدم ضمير المفعول her.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>They is students.</em> <strong>→ ✓ They are students.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الضمير they جمع فيأخذ are.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Yes, I'm.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Yes, I am.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نختصر الفعل في الإجابة القصيرة المثبتة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I → me · you → you · he → him · she → her</p>\n<p>it → it · we → us · they → them</p>\n<p>Subject: She helps us. Object: We help her.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the subject first: I → am, one person or thing → is, more than one → are.</p>\n<p>2. Two subjects joined by and are plural: Nasser and I are …</p>\n<p>3. Before the verb → subject pronoun; after a verb or preposition → object pronoun.</p>\n<p>4. In error identification, check every am / is / are against its subject, even when the subject is far away.</p>\n<p>5. Watch for an extra pronoun after a noun subject (My uncle he …) — a common STEP trap.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابدأ دائمًا بتحديد الفاعل، ثم اختر صورة فعل be المناسبة له، وتذكّر أن الضمير قبل الفعل يكون ضمير فاعل وبعد الفعل أو حرف الجر يكون ضمير مفعول.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Nasser and his cousin ______ in the same class.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. is B. am C. are D. be</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find the subject: Nasser and his cousin.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Two people joined by and = plural.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Plural subject + are. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل اسمان مربوطان بـ and فهو جمع، والجمع يأخذ are.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Our teacher gave ______ a new book.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. we B. us C. our D. ours</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The blank comes after the verb gave.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> After a verb we need an object pronoun.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The object pronoun of we is us. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد الفعل نحتاج ضمير مفعول، وضمير المفعول من we هو us.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>My</u> uncle (B) <u>he</u> (C) <u>is</u> a chef, and (D) <u>he</u> loves his job.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. My B. he C. is D. he</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The subject is My uncle.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> he after My uncle repeats the subject — this is wrong.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: My uncle is a chef, and he loves his job. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نكرر الفاعل بضمير بعد الاسم مباشرة.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 C · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I ______ a student at Al-Noor School.","o":["is","am","are","be"],"k":1,"e":"With I we always use am.","h":"مع الضمير I نستخدم am دائمًا."},{"n":2,"s":"Faisal ______ twelve years old.","o":["is","am","are","be"],"k":0,"e":"Faisal is one person (he), so the verb is is.","h":"الاسم المفرد يأخذ is."},{"n":3,"s":"______ are in the library now.","o":["They","Them","Their","He"],"k":0,"e":"Before the verb we need a subject pronoun, and are needs a plural subject: They.","h":"قبل الفعل نستخدم ضمير فاعل جمعًا مع are."},{"n":4,"s":"This pen is Omar's. Please give it to ______.","o":["he","his","him","they"],"k":2,"e":"After the preposition to we use an object pronoun; Omar → him.","h":"بعد حرف الجر to نستخدم ضمير المفعول him."},{"n":5,"s":"My grandmother is very kind. I love ______ very much.","o":["her","she","his","they"],"k":0,"e":"grandmother is the object of love, so we use her.","h":"الجدة مفعول به، فنستخدم her."},{"n":6,"s":"The weather ______ very hot in Riyadh in August.","o":["are","is","am","be"],"k":1,"e":"weather is singular, so it takes is.","h":"كلمة weather مفردة فتأخذ is."},{"n":7,"s":"______ is seven o'clock. Let's go.","o":["It","He","There","Its"],"k":0,"e":"We use It to talk about time.","h":"نستخدم It للحديث عن الوقت."},{"n":8,"s":"Mona and Reem ______ sisters.","o":["is","are","am","be"],"k":1,"e":"Two names joined by and are plural, so we use are.","h":"اسمان مع and يعنيان الجمع فنستخدم are."},{"n":9,"s":"\"Are you hungry?\" \"No, ______.\"","o":["I amn't","I not","I'm no","I'm not"],"k":3,"e":"The negative short answer with I is No, I'm not.","h":"النفي المختصر مع I هو I'm not."},{"n":10,"s":"\"Is your brother at home?\" \"Yes, ______.\"","o":["he's","it is","he is","him is"],"k":2,"e":"Positive short answers do not use contractions: Yes, he is.","h":"لا نختصر الفعل في الإجابة القصيرة المثبتة."},{"n":11,"s":"Our neighbours often help ______ with our garden.","o":["us","we","our","ours"],"k":0,"e":"After the verb help we need the object pronoun us.","h":"بعد الفعل help نستخدم ضمير المفعول us."},{"n":12,"s":"The students ______ not in the classroom; they are in the playground.","o":["are","is","am","be"],"k":0,"e":"The students is plural, so the negative is are not.","h":"الطلاب جمع فنستخدم are not."},{"n":13,"s":"My keys ______ in my bag. I can't find them.","o":["isn't","am not","aren't","not"],"k":2,"e":"keys is plural, so the negative is aren't.","h":"keys جمع فنفيه aren't."},{"n":14,"s":"______ your parents from Taif?","o":["Is","Am","Do","Are"],"k":3,"e":"The question has no main verb and the subject is plural, so we use Are.","h":"لا يوجد فعل آخر والفاعل جمع، فنبدأ السؤال بـ Are."},{"n":15,"s":"My friend and ______ are on the school football team.","o":["me","I","my","mine"],"k":1,"e":"The blank is part of the subject, so we use the subject pronoun I.","h":"الكلمة جزء من الفاعل فنستخدم I."},{"n":16,"s":"\"Where is Lina's bag?\" \"______ is under her desk.\"","o":["She","Her","They","It"],"k":3,"e":"A bag is a thing, so we use It.","h":"الحقيبة شيء مفرد فنستخدم It."},{"n":17,"s":"The teacher looked at Ali and ______ and smiled.","o":["I","me","my","mine"],"k":1,"e":"After the preposition at we use the object pronoun me.","h":"بعد at نستخدم ضمير المفعول me."},{"n":18,"s":"Sami's sisters and their cousin ______ at the park.","o":["is","am","are","be"],"k":2,"e":"The full subject (sisters and their cousin) is plural, so we use are, not is.","h":"الفاعل كله جمع، فلا ننظر إلى الكلمة الأخيرة فقط."},{"n":19,"s":"Hassan and Majed are late. Can you call ______?","o":["they","their","him","them"],"k":3,"e":"Two people as the object of call → them.","h":"شخصان في موضع المفعول فنستخدم them."},{"n":20,"s":"\"Is this your coat?\" \"No, it ______. My coat is black.\"","o":["aren't","am not","not is","isn't"],"k":3,"e":"it takes is; the negative is isn't.","h":"it يأخذ is ونفيه isn't."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"(A) My brother (B) are a doctor (C) in a big (D) hospital.","o":["My","are","in","hospital"],"k":1,"e":"My brother is singular, so the verb must be is.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) I (B) am fifteen, and my sister (C) she (D) is twelve.","o":["I","am","she","is"],"k":2,"e":"she repeats the subject my sister; it must be removed.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"Please (A) help (B) I with (C) this heavy (D) box.","o":["help","I","this","box"],"k":1,"e":"After the verb help we need the object pronoun me.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"The cats (A) is hungry, so (B) we give (C) them some (D) food.","o":["is","we","them","food"],"k":0,"e":"The cats is plural, so the verb must be are.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"Ahmed and (A) me (B) are in the (C) same class (D) this year.","o":["me","are","same","this"],"k":0,"e":"The pronoun is part of the subject, so it must be I.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"My mother (A) is a teacher, and (B) her students love (C) she very (D) much.","o":["is","her","she","much"],"k":2,"e":"she is the object of love, so it must be her.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) Are you and Omar ready? The bus (B) is here, and (C) it (D) are waiting for us.","o":["Are","is","it","are"],"k":3,"e":"it is singular, so the verb must be is.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) Is your father at work? Yes, (B) he's. (C) He (D) is an engineer.","o":["Is","he's","He","is"],"k":1,"e":"A positive short answer cannot end with a contraction: Yes, he is.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"The new students (A) are from Egypt, and (B) they (C) is very friendly to (D) us.","o":["are","they","is","us"],"k":2,"e":"they is plural, so the verb must be are.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) It is very cold (B) today, so my brothers and (C) I (D) am at home.","o":["It","today","I","am"],"k":3,"e":"my brothers and I is plural, so the verb must be are, not am.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.2","t":"Nouns: a / an, Plurals, Countable and Uncountable","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.2 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Choose a or an by the first sound of the next word, not the first letter (an hour, a university).</p>\n<p>2. Form regular and irregular plurals with correct spelling (-s, -es, -ies, -ves, children, women).</p>\n<p>3. Separate countable from uncountable nouns and avoid forms such as informations and advices.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يختار الطالب a أو an حسب الصوت الأول للكلمة التالية لا حسب الحرف المكتوب.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكوّن الجمع المنتظم والشاذ بتهجئة صحيحة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يميّز بين الأسماء المعدودة وغير المعدودة ويتجنب أخطاء مثل informations وadvices.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. I have ______ orange in my bag.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. a B. two C. an D. some</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. There are three ______ in the garden.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. children B. child C. childs D. childrens</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Can I have some ______, please?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. waters B. a water C. an water D. water</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>a + consonant SOUND</strong></p>\n<p><strong>a book · a car · a university /ju/ · a one-day trip /w/</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. My cousin has a uniform for school.</em></p>\n<p><strong>an + vowel SOUND</strong></p>\n<p><strong>an apple · an egg · an umbrella · an hour (silent h)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We waited for an hour.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Plural: most nouns + s</strong></p>\n<p><strong>book → books · car → cars · day → days · key → keys</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Two days ago I lost my keys.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Plural: -s, -ss, -sh, -ch, -x, -o + es</strong></p>\n<p><strong>bus → buses · class → classes · dish → dishes · watch → watches · box → boxes · tomato → tomatoes</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The boxes are in the kitchen.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Plural: consonant + y → -ies</strong></p>\n<p><strong>city → cities · baby → babies · story → stories</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Riyadh and Dammam are big cities.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Plural: -f / -fe → -ves</strong></p>\n<p><strong>leaf → leaves · knife → knives · wife → wives · shelf → shelves</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The leaves are green.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Irregular plurals</strong></p>\n<p><strong>man → men · woman → women · child → children · person → people · foot → feet · tooth → teeth · mouse → mice</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Three women are in the waiting room.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Same in singular and plural</strong></p>\n<p><strong>sheep → sheep · fish → fish</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. My uncle has ten sheep.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Uncountable nouns (no a / an, no -s, singular verb)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>water · rice · bread · money · information · advice · homework · furniture · luggage · news</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The news is good. My homework is easy.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Counting uncountable nouns</strong></p>\n<p><strong>a glass of water · a cup of tea · a piece of advice · a kilo of rice · a loaf of bread</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Can I have a glass of water, please?</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. a / an = one; first mention; jobs.</strong></p>\n<p>We use a or an with one singular countable noun, when we mention it for the first time, and with jobs.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I can see a camel near the road.</p>\n<p>▸ My uncle is an engineer.</p>\n<p>▸ Mariam has an old phone.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Plural nouns = more than one.</strong></p>\n<p>Countable nouns have a plural form. We use numbers and words like many and a lot of with them.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Two buses stop in front of our school.</p>\n<p>▸ The children are in the garden.</p>\n<p>▸ We have many classes on Sunday.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Uncountable nouns take a singular verb.</strong></p>\n<p>Uncountable nouns are things we cannot count one by one. They have no plural and take is / was.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The news is very good today.</p>\n<p>▸ Rice is cheap at this market.</p>\n<p>▸ Your advice is useful.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Units make uncountable nouns countable.</strong></p>\n<p>To count uncountable things, we use a unit or container + of.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Two cups of tea, please.</p>\n<p>▸ She gave me two pieces of advice.</p>\n<p>▸ We need a kilo of rice and a bottle of oil.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Listen to the SOUND: a university /juː/, a European city /j/, an honest man (silent h), an hour.</p>\n<p>▸ Plural -s is pronounced /s/ (books), /z/ (days) or /ɪz/ (boxes, buses).</p>\n<p>▸ people is plural: People are friendly here. (not People is)</p>\n<p>▸ Exceptions to -f → -ves: roof → roofs, chief → chiefs.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم a قبل الكلمة التي تبدأ بصوت ساكن، وan قبل الكلمة التي تبدأ بصوت متحرك، والعبرة بالصوت لا بالحرف؛ لذلك نقول a university لأنها تبدأ بصوت (يو)، ونقول an hour لأن حرف h لا يُنطق.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نكوّن الجمع غالبًا بإضافة s، ونضيف es بعد s وsh وch وx وo، ونغيّر y إلى ies إذا سبقها حرف ساكن، ونغيّر f أو fe إلى ves. وهناك جموع شاذة يجب حفظها مثل children وpeople وteeth.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأسماء غير المعدودة مثل water وinformation وadvice وhomework لا تأخذ a أو an ولا تُجمع، ويأتي بعدها فعل مفرد. وإذا أردنا عدّها استخدمنا وحدة مثل a piece of أو a glass of.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>an university</em> <strong>→ ✓ a university</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العبرة بالصوت؛ university تبدأ بصوت (يو) الساكن.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He is engineer.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He is an engineer.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في العربية لا نضع أداة قبل المهنة، أما في الإنجليزية فنضع a أو an.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>informations / advices</em> <strong>→ ✓ information / advice</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">هذه الأسماء غير معدودة في الإنجليزية وإن كانت تُجمع في العربية.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>two child / childrens</em> <strong>→ ✓ two children</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">children جمع شاذ ولا نضيف إليه s.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The news are good.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The news is good.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">كلمة news مفردة رغم انتهائها بحرف s.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>a homework</em> <strong>→ ✓ some homework / a piece of homework</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">homework غير معدودة فلا تأخذ a.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Countable: a book · two books · many books · How many books?</p>\n<p>Uncountable: some water · a lot of water · a glass of water · How much water?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Look at the word right after the blank: is it countable or uncountable, singular or plural?</p>\n<p>2. For a / an, say the next word aloud and listen to its first sound.</p>\n<p>3. A number (two, three) before the blank means a plural noun; much, a little or some + singular verb suggests an uncountable noun.</p>\n<p>4. Check plural spelling carefully: -ies, -ves and irregular forms are favourite STEP traps.</p>\n<p>5. Words like information, advice, news, luggage and furniture never take -s.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">انظر إلى الكلمة التي بعد الفراغ: هل هي معدودة أم غير معدودة؟ مفردة أم جمع؟ ثم انطق الكلمة لتختار a أو an، وراجع تهجئة الجمع جيدًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. My father is ______ honest man.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. a B. an C. two D. some</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The next word is honest.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The h in honest is silent, so the first sound is a vowel sound.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Vowel sound → an. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حرف h في honest لا يُنطق فتبدأ الكلمة بصوت متحرك، لذلك نستخدم an.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. We need some ______ about the trip.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. informations B. an information C. information D. a informations</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> information is uncountable.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Uncountable nouns have no -s and no a / an.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">information اسم غير معدود فلا يُجمع ولا يأخذ a أو an.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. There are three (A) <u>big</u> (B) <u>bags</u> and two (C) <u>box</u> of (D) <u>books</u> in the car.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. big B. bags C. box D. books</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> two tells us we need a plural noun.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The plural of box is boxes (-x + es).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: There are three big bags and two boxes of books in the car. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد العدد two نحتاج الجمع، وجمع box هو boxes.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 D · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 C · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I eat ______ apple every morning.","o":["an","a","two","some"],"k":0,"e":"apple starts with a vowel sound, so we use an.","h":"apple تبدأ بصوت متحرك فنستخدم an."},{"n":2,"s":"My cousin has ______ new bicycle.","o":["an","two","some","a"],"k":3,"e":"new starts with a consonant sound, so we use a.","h":"الكلمة التالية new تبدأ بصوت ساكن فنستخدم a."},{"n":3,"s":"There are two ______ in the kitchen.","o":["chair","chaires","a chair","chairs"],"k":3,"e":"two needs a plural noun: chairs.","h":"بعد two نستخدم الجمع."},{"n":4,"s":"Five ______ are playing football in the street.","o":["boy","boys","boyes","a boy"],"k":1,"e":"boy ends in vowel + y, so we just add -s: boys.","h":"boy تنتهي بحرف متحرك + y فنضيف s فقط."},{"n":5,"s":"Put the pens in those two ______.","o":["boxes","box","boxs","boxies"],"k":0,"e":"Nouns ending in -x add -es: boxes.","h":"الكلمة المنتهية بـ x نضيف إليها es."},{"n":6,"s":"Our new teacher is ______ Egyptian.","o":["a","two","an","some"],"k":2,"e":"Egyptian starts with a vowel sound, so we use an.","h":"Egyptian تبدأ بصوت متحرك فنستخدم an."},{"n":7,"s":"I would like a glass of ______.","o":["waters","a water","water","an water"],"k":2,"e":"water is uncountable: a glass of water.","h":"water غير معدودة فلا تُجمع."},{"n":8,"s":"Riyadh and Jeddah are big ______.","o":["city","cities","citys","cityes"],"k":1,"e":"Consonant + y changes to -ies: cities.","h":"حرف ساكن + y يتحول إلى ies."},{"n":9,"s":"My little brother has two loose ______.","o":["teeth","tooth","tooths","teeths"],"k":0,"e":"The plural of tooth is the irregular form teeth.","h":"جمع tooth الشاذ هو teeth."},{"n":10,"s":"We waited for ______ hour at the airport.","o":["a","two","many","an"],"k":3,"e":"The h in hour is silent, so the first sound is a vowel: an hour.","h":"حرف h في hour لا يُنطق فنستخدم an."},{"n":11,"s":"My mother bought two kilos of ______ from the market.","o":["rices","rice","a rice","an rice"],"k":1,"e":"rice is uncountable; the unit kilos is plural, not rice.","h":"rice غير معدودة، والجمع يكون للوحدة kilos."},{"n":12,"s":"Can you give me some ______ about the test?","o":["informations","an information","information","a information"],"k":2,"e":"information is uncountable: no -s, no a / an.","h":"information غير معدودة."},{"n":13,"s":"There are many ______ in the park on Fridays.","o":["peoples","person","persones","people"],"k":3,"e":"The plural of person is people.","h":"جمع person هو people."},{"n":14,"s":"My uncle is ______ university teacher in Abha.","o":["an","two","some","a"],"k":3,"e":"university starts with the sound /ju/, a consonant sound, so we use a.","h":"university تبدأ بصوت (يو) الساكن فنستخدم a."},{"n":15,"s":"The ______ are in the drawer next to the spoons.","o":["knifes","knives","knife","knivs"],"k":1,"e":"knife → knives (-fe changes to -ves).","h":"knife يصبح knives في الجمع."},{"n":16,"s":"My sister has ______ homework tonight.","o":["many","a","a lot of","an"],"k":2,"e":"homework is uncountable, so we use a lot of, not many or a / an.","h":"homework غير معدودة فنستخدم a lot of."},{"n":17,"s":"The farmer has twenty ______ and ten goats.","o":["sheeps","sheepes","a sheep","sheep"],"k":3,"e":"sheep has the same form in the singular and the plural.","h":"كلمة sheep لا تتغير في الجمع."},{"n":18,"s":"I need two ______ of paper for my drawing.","o":["piece","peaces","a piece","pieces"],"k":3,"e":"We count paper with pieces; two needs the plural pieces.","h":"نعدّ الورق بـ pieces، وبعد two نستخدم الجمع."},{"n":19,"s":"The ______ on the trees are green in spring.","o":["leaves","leafs","leaf","leavs"],"k":0,"e":"leaf → leaves (-f changes to -ves).","h":"leaf يصبح leaves."},{"n":20,"s":"Your ______ is very useful. Thank you!","o":["advices","an advice","advice","a advices"],"k":2,"e":"advice is uncountable and takes a singular verb (is).","h":"advice غير معدودة ويأتي بعدها is."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"I have (A) a brother and (B) two (C) sister at (D) home.","o":["a","two","sister","home"],"k":2,"e":"two needs a plural noun: sisters.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"We saw (A) a elephant and three (B) monkeys at (C) the (D) zoo.","o":["a","monkeys","the","zoo"],"k":0,"e":"elephant starts with a vowel sound, so it needs an.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"My father (A) is (B) a engineer, and he (C) works in (D) a big company.","o":["is","a","works","a"],"k":1,"e":"engineer starts with a vowel sound: an engineer.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"There (A) are three new (B) buses in front of (C) the school (D) every mornings.","o":["are","buses","the","every mornings"],"k":3,"e":"After every we use a singular noun: every morning.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"She gave me (A) some good (B) advices about (C) my English (D) test.","o":["some","advices","my","test"],"k":1,"e":"advice is uncountable, so it has no -s.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"The (A) childrens in (B) my class (C) are (D) very friendly.","o":["childrens","my","are","very"],"k":0,"e":"children is already plural; it never takes -s.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) The news (B) are (C) very good (D) today.","o":["The","are","very","today"],"k":1,"e":"news is uncountable and singular, so the verb is is.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) My mother needs (B) two (C) kilo of rice from (D) the market.","o":["My","two","kilo","the"],"k":2,"e":"two needs the plural unit kilos.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) My grandparents have (B) a farm with many (C) sheeps and (D) cows.","o":["My","a","sheeps","cows"],"k":2,"e":"The plural of sheep is sheep.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"Is there (A) an (B) university near (C) your (D) house?","o":["an","university","your","house"],"k":0,"e":"university starts with the consonant sound /ju/, so we use a.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.3","t":"Possessive Adjectives, Possessive 's and this / that / these / those","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.3 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use my, your, his, her, its, our and their correctly, and tell its from it's.</p>\n<p>2. Form the possessive 's and s' for singular and plural owners.</p>\n<p>3. Match this, that, these and those to number (one / many) and distance (near / far).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب صفات الملكية استخدامًا صحيحًا ويميّز بين its وit's.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكوّن الملكية بـ 's و s' للمالك المفرد والجمع.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يختار this أو that أو these أو those حسب العدد والمسافة.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. This is ______ bag. I bought it yesterday.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. me B. I C. mine D. my</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. These ______ my books.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. is B. are C. am D. be</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. The ______ car is red. (one teacher)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. teacher's B. teachers C. teacher D. teachers'</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Possessive adjectives + noun</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I → my · you → your · he → his · she → her · it → its · we → our · they → their</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. This is my phone. Their house is new.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Singular owner + 's</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Ali → Ali's book · my sister → my sister's room</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. My sister's room is tidy.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Plural owner ending in -s + '</strong></p>\n<p><strong>the students → the students' books · my parents → my parents' car</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. My parents' car is white.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Irregular plural owner + 's</strong></p>\n<p><strong>children → the children's toys · men → the men's room · people → people's ideas</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The children's toys are on the floor.</em></p>\n<p><strong>this / these (near)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>this + singular noun · these + plural noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. This cup is hot. These dates are fresh.</em></p>\n<p><strong>that / those (far)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>that + singular noun · those + plural noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. That building is a hospital. Those birds are eagles.</em></p>\n<p><strong>its vs it's</strong></p>\n<p><strong>its = belonging to it · it's = it is / it has</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The cat is eating its food. It's very hungry.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Possessive adjectives show who something belongs to.</strong></p>\n<p>They always come before a noun. The word depends on the OWNER, not on the thing.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Fahad is washing his car.</p>\n<p>▸ Noura is reading her book.</p>\n<p>▸ We love our school.</p>\n<p>▸ The tree has lost its leaves.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. 's shows the owner with names and nouns.</strong></p>\n<p>English uses 's where Arabic uses the idafa structure (كتاب علي).</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ This is Ali's book.</p>\n<p>▸ My brother's school is near our house.</p>\n<p>▸ The students' bags are in the classroom.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. this / these point to things near us; that / those point to things far away.</strong></p>\n<p>Use this and that with one thing; use these and those with more than one.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ This sandwich is delicious.</p>\n<p>▸ These shoes are too small.</p>\n<p>▸ Look at that mountain!</p>\n<p>▸ Those men are firefighters.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. this / that / these / those can stand alone.</strong></p>\n<p>They can also be used without a noun.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ This is my cousin, Hamad.</p>\n<p>▸ Are those your keys?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ his = the owner is a man or boy; her = the owner is a woman or girl — even if the thing is male or female: Maha loves her father.</p>\n<p>▸ Never write it's for possession. Test: can you say it is? If not, write its.</p>\n<p>▸ their (possession) · there (place) · they're (they are) sound the same but are spelled differently.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">صفة الملكية تأتي قبل الاسم وتتبع المالك لا الشيء المملوك؛ فنقول Maha loves her father لأن المالكة أنثى، ونقول Ali loves his mother لأن المالك ذكر.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نعبّر عن الملكية مع الأسماء بإضافة 's إلى المالك المفرد مثل Ali's book، وبإضافة الفاصلة العليا فقط بعد الجمع المنتهي بـ s مثل the students' books، أما الجمع الشاذ فيأخذ 's مثل the children's toys.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم this وthese للقريب، وthat وthose للبعيد؛ this وthat مع المفرد، وthese وthose مع الجمع. وتذكّر أن its تعني (ـه أو ـها لغير العاقل) بينما it's اختصار it is.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>This is the book of Ali.</em> <strong>→ ✓ This is Ali's book.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تركيب الإضافة العربي يُعبَّر عنه في الإنجليزية بـ 's.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Maha loves his father.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Maha loves her father.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نختار his أو her حسب المالك لا حسب الشيء المملوك.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>These book is mine.</em> <strong>→ ✓ This book is mine.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">these للجمع فقط، ومع المفرد نستخدم this.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The dog is eating it's food.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The dog is eating its food.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">it's تعني it is، أما الملكية فهي its.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>my fathers car</em> <strong>→ ✓ my father's car</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا بد من الفاصلة العليا مع s للدلالة على الملكية.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Their are my cousins.</em> <strong>→ ✓ They are my cousins.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">their للملكية وليست فعلًا أو ضميرًا فاعلًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>his / her → follow the owner: Ali's sister → his sister · Huda's brother → her brother</p>\n<p>its / it's: The shop opens its doors at 9. · It's (= It is) open now.</p>\n<p>this / that / these / those: near + one → this · far + one → that · near + many → these · far + many → those</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. For his / her / their, ask: who is the OWNER? Then choose the possessive.</p>\n<p>2. For this / these / that / those, check the noun after the blank: singular or plural?</p>\n<p>3. For 's or s', ask: one owner or many? Is the plural irregular (children, men)?</p>\n<p>4. If you see it's, replace it with it is. If the sentence breaks, the correct word is its.</p>\n<p>5. STEP likes confusing pairs: its / it's, their / there / they're, your / you're.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد المالك أولًا لتختار صفة الملكية، وانظر إلى الاسم بعد الفراغ لتعرف هل هو مفرد أو جمع، وجرّب استبدال it's بـ it is لتتأكد من الاختيار.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Noura is washing ______ hands before lunch.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. his B. its C. her D. their</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The owner of the hands is Noura.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Noura is a girl, so we use her.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المالكة هي نورة فنستخدم her.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. ______ boys over there are my cousins.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. This B. Those C. That D. These</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> boys is plural.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> over there means far.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Plural + far = Those. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الاسم جمع وبعيد فنستخدم Those.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>This</u> is (B) <u>my</u> (C) <u>sister</u> car, and (D) <u>it</u> is new.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. This B. my C. sister D. it</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The car belongs to my sister.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We need the possessive form sister's.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: This is my sister's car, and it is new. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للتعبير عن الملكية نضيف 's إلى المالك.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 D · 2 B · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I love ______ school. It is very beautiful.","o":["me","I","my","mine"],"k":2,"e":"Before a noun we use the possessive adjective my.","h":"قبل الاسم نستخدم صفة الملكية my."},{"n":2,"s":"Ahmed is cleaning ______ room.","o":["his","he","him","her"],"k":0,"e":"The owner is Ahmed (a boy), so we use his.","h":"المالك ذكر فنستخدم his."},{"n":3,"s":"______ pen on my desk is new.","o":["These","Those","This","They"],"k":2,"e":"pen is singular and near (on my desk): This.","h":"مفرد وقريب فنستخدم This."},{"n":4,"s":"We like ______ teacher very much.","o":["us","our","we","ours"],"k":1,"e":"Before the noun teacher we use our.","h":"قبل الاسم نستخدم our."},{"n":5,"s":"Look at ______ birds high in the sky!","o":["those","that","this","them"],"k":0,"e":"birds is plural and far away: those.","h":"جمع وبعيد فنستخدم those."},{"n":6,"s":"Hessa is in ______ bedroom. She is reading.","o":["his","she","hers","her"],"k":3,"e":"The owner is Hessa, so we use her.","h":"المالكة أنثى فنستخدم her."},{"n":7,"s":"This bike belongs to Sami. It is ______ bike.","o":["Samis","Sami's","Sami","Samis'"],"k":1,"e":"One owner + 's: Sami's bike.","h":"المالك مفرد فنضيف 's."},{"n":8,"s":"______ apples in my hand are fresh.","o":["This","That","There","These"],"k":3,"e":"apples is plural and near (in my hand): These.","h":"جمع وقريب فنستخدم These."},{"n":9,"s":"My parents are at ______ friend's house.","o":["there","they","their","them"],"k":2,"e":"Before a noun phrase we need the possessive adjective their.","h":"قبل الاسم نستخدم their للملكية."},{"n":10,"s":"The cat is playing with ______ toy.","o":["it's","it","its'","its"],"k":3,"e":"Possession for an animal or thing is its (no apostrophe).","h":"الملكية لغير العاقل its بلا فاصلة."},{"n":11,"s":"Do you like ______ new shoes? I bought them yesterday.","o":["my","me","mine","I"],"k":0,"e":"Before the noun shoes we use my.","h":"قبل الاسم نستخدم my."},{"n":12,"s":"The ______ toys are in the garden.","o":["children's","childrens'","childrens","children"],"k":0,"e":"children is an irregular plural, so it takes 's: children's.","h":"الجمع الشاذ children يأخذ 's."},{"n":13,"s":"Is ______ your coat over there on the chair?","o":["this","these","those","that"],"k":3,"e":"One coat, far away (over there): that.","h":"مفرد وبعيد فنستخدم that."},{"n":14,"s":"My brother and I share a room. ______ room is small but nice.","o":["Their","My","Our","We"],"k":2,"e":"The owners are my brother and I = we, so we use Our.","h":"المالكان أنا وأخي فنستخدم Our."},{"n":15,"s":"Rana's father is a pilot. ______ name is Saad.","o":["Her","Its","Their","His"],"k":3,"e":"The name belongs to the father (a man), so we use His.","h":"الاسم للأب فنستخدم His."},{"n":16,"s":"The teachers are in ______ meeting room now.","o":["there","their","they're","them"],"k":1,"e":"The room belongs to the teachers: their.","h":"الغرفة للمعلمين فنستخدم their."},{"n":17,"s":"My uncle has two sons. ______ names are Fahad and Turki.","o":["Their","His","There","They're"],"k":0,"e":"The names belong to the two sons (they), so we use Their.","h":"الأسماء للابنين فنستخدم Their."},{"n":18,"s":"I can't find ______ keys. Did you see them?","o":["me","mine","my","mines"],"k":2,"e":"Before the noun keys we use my.","h":"قبل الاسم نستخدم my."},{"n":19,"s":"The ______ office is on the second floor. He is there now.","o":["manager's","managers","manager","managers's"],"k":0,"e":"One manager (he) + 's: manager's.","h":"مدير واحد فنضيف 's."},{"n":20,"s":"It's a nice hotel, but ______ rooms are small.","o":["it's","its","his","it"],"k":1,"e":"The rooms belong to the hotel, so we use its; it's means it is.","h":"الملكية للفندق its، أما it's فتعني it is."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"(A) This (B) are my cousin, and (C) his name is (D) Bader.","o":["This","are","his","Bader"],"k":1,"e":"This is singular, so the verb must be is.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"Maha visits (A) his grandmother (B) every Friday with (C) her (D) brother.","o":["his","every","her","brother"],"k":0,"e":"The owner is Maha, so we need her.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"Look at (A) those (B) camel over there near (C) the (D) trees.","o":["those","camel","the","trees"],"k":1,"e":"those needs a plural noun: camels.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"The (A) teachers room is (B) next to (C) our (D) classroom.","o":["teachers","next to","our","classroom"],"k":0,"e":"The room belongs to the teachers, so we need teachers'.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"My (A) brother's friends (B) are nice, and I like (C) all (D) theirs parents.","o":["brother's","are","all","theirs"],"k":3,"e":"Before the noun parents we need their, not theirs.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"(A) Our dog is sleeping (B) in the garden, but (C) it's bed is (D) in the kitchen.","o":["Our","in","it's","in"],"k":2,"e":"Possession needs its; it's means it is.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"Is (A) this (B) your phone, or is it (C) you (D) brother's?","o":["this","your","you","brother's"],"k":2,"e":"Before brother's we need the possessive your.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) These are my (B) parents car keys; please give (C) them to (D) my father.","o":["These","parents","them","my"],"k":1,"e":"The keys belong to my parents, so we need parents'.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Those flowers in (B) your garden are lovely. What (C) are (D) they're names?","o":["Those","your","are","they're"],"k":3,"e":"Possession needs their; they're means they are.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"My (A) sister's friends (B) visit (C) she every (D) weekend.","o":["sister's","visit","she","weekend"],"k":2,"e":"After the verb visit we need the object pronoun her.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.4","t":"There is / There are and have got / has got","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.4 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use there is / there are with singular, plural and uncountable nouns.</p>\n<p>2. Form have got / has got in positive, negative and question forms, with short answers.</p>\n<p>3. Avoid Arabic-influenced errors such as There have a park and In my city have …</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب there is وthere are مع الأسماء المفردة والجمع وغير المعدودة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكوّن have got وhas got في الإثبات والنفي والسؤال مع الإجابات القصيرة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يتجنب الأخطاء المتأثرة بالعربية مثل There have a park.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. There ______ a park near my house.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. are B. is C. am D. have</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. My sister ______ got long hair.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. have B. is C. does D. has</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. ______ there any milk in the fridge?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Is B. Are C. Has D. Have</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>There is + singular / uncountable</strong></p>\n<p><strong>There is + a / an + noun · There is + some + uncountable noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. There is a mosque near the school. There is some water in the jug.</em></p>\n<p><strong>There are + plural</strong></p>\n<p><strong>There are + number / some / many / a lot of + plural noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. There are two banks on this street.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>There isn't a … / There isn't any + uncountable · There aren't any + plural</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. There isn't any bread. There aren't any buses after midnight.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Questions and short answers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Is there a / any …? — Yes, there is. / No, there isn't. Are there any …? — Yes, there are. / No, there aren't.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Are there any shops here? Yes, there are.</em></p>\n<p><strong>have got — positive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I / you / we / they + have got ('ve got) · he / she / it + has got ('s got)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I've got a new watch. She's got two brothers.</em></p>\n<p><strong>have got — negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>haven't got · hasn't got</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We haven't got a car. He hasn't got a phone.</em></p>\n<p><strong>have got — questions and short answers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Have / Has + subject + got …? — Yes, I have. / No, she hasn't.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Have you got a pen? Yes, I have.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. There is / there are say that something exists in a place.</strong></p>\n<p>We use them to describe a place or to say what is (or is not) somewhere.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ There is a big supermarket near our house.</p>\n<p>▸ There are thirty students in my class.</p>\n<p>▸ There isn't any juice in the fridge.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. have got / has got show possession, family and appearance.</strong></p>\n<p>We use have got for things we own, people in our family, and how people look.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My uncle has got a farm in Al-Qassim.</p>\n<p>▸ We've got three cousins in Madinah.</p>\n<p>▸ Turki has got short black hair.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. have got for illnesses.</strong></p>\n<p>We also use it for simple health problems.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I've got a cold.</p>\n<p>▸ She has got a headache today.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. have (without got) is also correct.</strong></p>\n<p>In questions and negatives with have (no got), we use do / does.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Do you have a pen? (= Have you got a pen?)</p>\n<p>▸ He doesn't have a car. (= He hasn't got a car.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Do not mix the two patterns: ✗ Do you have got …? ✓ Have you got …? / Do you have …?</p>\n<p>▸ Short answers with have got do not repeat got: Yes, I have. (not Yes, I have got.)</p>\n<p>▸ There is and It is are different: There is a book on the desk. It is my book.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم there is مع الاسم المفرد وغير المعدود، وthere are مع الاسم الجمع، للتعبير عن وجود شيء في مكان ما، وهي تقابل «يوجد» في العربية. وفي النفي نقول there isn't وthere aren't، وفي السؤال نقدّم is أو are على there.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم have got مع I وyou وwe وthey، وhas got مع he وshe وit، للتعبير عن الملكية والعائلة والمظهر. وفي السؤال نبدأ بـ Have أو Has، وفي الإجابة القصيرة لا نكرر كلمة got.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا تترجم «يوجد» أو «عندنا» حرفيًا إلى have؛ فالجملة There have a park خاطئة، والصحيح There is a park.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>There have a big park in my city.</em> <strong>→ ✓ There is a big park in my city.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">«يوجد» في الإنجليزية there is وليس there have.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>In my school have many classes.</em> <strong>→ ✓ There are many classes in my school.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نبدأ الجملة بـ have دون فاعل كما في «في مدرستي عندنا».</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>There is many cars.</em> <strong>→ ✓ There are many cars.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الاسم الجمع يأخذ there are.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She have got a cat.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She has got a cat.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">she تأخذ has.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Yes, I have got.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Yes, I have.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نكرر got في الإجابة القصيرة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It has a lot of shops in Riyadh.</em> <strong>→ ✓ There are a lot of shops in Riyadh.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للتعبير عن الوجود في مكان نستخدم there are لا it has.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Place → There is / There are: There is a pool in our school.</p>\n<p>Owner → have got / has got: Our school has got a pool.</p>\n<p>Existence vs identity: There is a car outside. It is my father's car.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Look at the noun after the blank: singular or uncountable → is; plural → are.</p>\n<p>2. Words like many, a lot of, two, some + plural noun → there are.</p>\n<p>3. For have got, find the subject: he / she / it or a singular name → has got.</p>\n<p>4. Questions with there: Is there …? / Are there …? — check the noun that follows.</p>\n<p>5. STEP error items often use the Arabic-style There have … or It has … for existence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">انظر إلى الاسم بعد الفراغ لتختار is أو are، وحدّد الفاعل لتختار have أو has، وتذكّر أن «يوجد» تُترجم there is أو there are.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. There ______ some juice in the bottle.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. are B. have C. is D. has</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> juice is uncountable.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Uncountable nouns take there is.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">juice غير معدودة فنستخدم there is.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. My cousins ______ got a big house in Abha.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. has B. have C. are D. is</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The subject my cousins is plural (they).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> they + have got.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل جمع فيأخذ have got.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Near (A) <u>our</u> school (B) <u>there</u> (C) <u>are</u> a new (D) <u>shop</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. our B. there C. are D. shop</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The noun is a new shop — singular.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Singular needs There is.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: Near our school there is a new shop. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الاسم مفرد فنستخدم There is.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 D · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"There ______ a computer in my room.","o":["are","am","have","is"],"k":3,"e":"a computer is singular: There is.","h":"الاسم مفرد فنستخدم There is."},{"n":2,"s":"There ______ four people in my family.","o":["is","am","are","has"],"k":2,"e":"four people is plural: There are.","h":"الاسم جمع فنستخدم There are."},{"n":3,"s":"I ______ got a new bicycle.","o":["has","am","is","have"],"k":3,"e":"With I we use have got.","h":"مع I نستخدم have got."},{"n":4,"s":"My sister ______ got a white cat.","o":["have","is","has","does"],"k":2,"e":"My sister = she, so we use has got.","h":"الفاعل مفرد مؤنث فنستخدم has got."},{"n":5,"s":"______ there a bank near here?","o":["Are","Has","Is","Have"],"k":2,"e":"a bank is singular: Is there …?","h":"الاسم مفرد فيبدأ السؤال بـ Is."},{"n":6,"s":"There aren't ______ eggs in the fridge.","o":["any","some","a","an"],"k":0,"e":"In negatives with plural nouns we use any.","h":"في النفي مع الجمع نستخدم any."},{"n":7,"s":"\"Have you got a pencil?\" \"Yes, I ______.\"","o":["has","have","got","do"],"k":1,"e":"The short answer to Have you got …? is Yes, I have.","h":"الإجابة القصيرة Yes, I have."},{"n":8,"s":"There ______ some milk on the table.","o":["are","have","has","is"],"k":3,"e":"milk is uncountable: There is.","h":"milk غير معدودة فنستخدم There is."},{"n":9,"s":"Our school ______ got a big library.","o":["have","is","are","has"],"k":3,"e":"Our school = it, so we use has got.","h":"المدرسة مفردة فنستخدم has got."},{"n":10,"s":"______ there any good restaurants in your town?","o":["Is","Have","Are","Do"],"k":2,"e":"restaurants is plural: Are there …?","h":"الاسم جمع فيبدأ السؤال بـ Are."},{"n":11,"s":"My grandfather ______ got a car; he walks everywhere.","o":["haven't","isn't","doesn't","hasn't"],"k":3,"e":"My grandfather = he → hasn't got.","h":"الفاعل مفرد فننفي بـ hasn't got."},{"n":12,"s":"______ a lot of traffic in Riyadh in the morning.","o":["There is","It is","There are","It has"],"k":0,"e":"traffic is uncountable, and we talk about existence: There is.","h":"traffic غير معدودة، وللوجود نستخدم There is."},{"n":13,"s":"______ your parents got a car?","o":["Has","Are","Have","Do"],"k":2,"e":"your parents = they → Have … got?","h":"الفاعل جمع فيبدأ السؤال بـ Have."},{"n":14,"s":"There ______ any students in the classroom now. It's break time.","o":["isn't","aren't","haven't","don't"],"k":1,"e":"students is plural, so the negative is There aren't.","h":"الاسم جمع فننفي بـ aren't."},{"n":15,"s":"\"Is there any bread?\" \"Yes, ______.\"","o":["there are","there is","it is","it has"],"k":1,"e":"The short answer to Is there …? is Yes, there is.","h":"الإجابة القصيرة Yes, there is."},{"n":16,"s":"Jeddah ______ a long beach called the Corniche.","o":["have","there is","has","is"],"k":2,"e":"Jeddah is the owner (singular) → has.","h":"جدة مفرد فتأخذ has."},{"n":17,"s":"How many rooms ______ in your new flat?","o":["there are","are there","is there","has there"],"k":1,"e":"A question with How many + plural noun uses are there.","h":"في السؤال مع How many نستخدم are there."},{"n":18,"s":"My friends and I ______ got a lot of homework this week.","o":["have","has","are","is"],"k":0,"e":"My friends and I = we, so we use have got.","h":"الفاعل المركب يساوي we فنستخدم have."},{"n":19,"s":"There ______ much water in the bottle. Please fill it.","o":["aren't","isn't","hasn't","haven't"],"k":1,"e":"water is uncountable, so the negative is There isn't.","h":"water غير معدودة فننفي بـ isn't."},{"n":20,"s":"______ any juice left? I'm thirsty.","o":["Are there","There is","Has it","Is there"],"k":3,"e":"juice is uncountable, and questions put is before there: Is there …?","h":"في السؤال نقدّم is على there، وjuice غير معدودة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"(A) There (B) is two (C) big trees in (D) our garden.","o":["There","is","big","our"],"k":1,"e":"two trees is plural, so we need There are.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"My brother (A) have (B) got a new (C) watch from (D) our uncle.","o":["have","got","watch","our"],"k":0,"e":"My brother = he, so the verb is has got.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"(A) Is there (B) any (C) apples in (D) the basket?","o":["Is","any","apples","the"],"k":0,"e":"apples is plural, so the question starts with Are.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"(A) In my city (B) have many (C) parks and (D) malls.","o":["In","have","parks","malls"],"k":1,"e":"To show that something exists, we use there are, not have.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"There is a lot of (A) traffic here, (B) so there (C) are a lot of (D) noise too.","o":["traffic","so","are","noise"],"k":2,"e":"noise is uncountable, so we need there is.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"We (A) haven't got (B) some milk, so let's (C) go to (D) the shop.","o":["haven't","some","go","the"],"k":1,"e":"In negative sentences we use any, not some.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"There (A) isn't (B) any chairs in (C) the room, so we (D) can't sit.","o":["isn't","any","the","can't"],"k":0,"e":"chairs is plural, so the negative is There aren't.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) Have your brothers (B) got a ball? No, they (C) haven't. They (D) has a kite.","o":["Have","got","haven't","has"],"k":3,"e":"They takes have, not has.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) It has a lot of (B) shops and (C) cafés (D) in Al-Khobar.","o":["It has","shops","cafés","in"],"k":0,"e":"For existence in a place we use There are, not It has.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"Our teacher (A) has got (B) two daughters, but (C) she hasn't got (D) some sons.","o":["has","two","she","some"],"k":3,"e":"In negative sentences we use any, not some.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.5","t":"Present Simple (All Forms and Wh- Questions) and Adverbs of Frequency","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.5 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Form the present simple, including third-person -s / -es and do / does in questions and negatives.</p>\n<p>2. Ask and answer Wh- questions in the present simple.</p>\n<p>3. Place adverbs of frequency before the main verb and after be.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكوّن الطالب المضارع البسيط بما في ذلك إضافة s/es مع الغائب المفرد، واستخدام do وdoes في السؤال والنفي.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يطرح أسئلة Wh- في المضارع البسيط ويجيب عنها.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يضع ظروف التكرار قبل الفعل الرئيس وبعد فعل be.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. She ______ tea every morning.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. drink B. drinks C. drinking D. is drink</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. ______ you like football?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Does B. Are C. Is D. Do</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. I ______ late for school.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. never am B. never is C. am never D. is never</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Positive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I / you / we / they + base verb · he / she / it + verb + -s / -es</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I live in Taif. My brother lives in Riyadh.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I / you / we / they + don't + base verb · he / she / it + doesn't + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We don't eat fast food. She doesn't drive.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Yes / No questions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Do / Does + subject + base verb …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Do you speak English? Does your father work on Saturdays?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Short answers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Yes, I do. / No, I don't. · Yes, he does. / No, he doesn't.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Does she like cats? No, she doesn't.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Wh- questions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Wh- word + do / does + subject + base verb …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Where do you live? What time does the bus leave?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Subject questions (no do / does)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Who / What + verb + -s …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Who lives in this house? What happens next?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adverbs of frequency</strong></p>\n<p><strong>always (100%) · usually · often · sometimes · rarely · never (0%)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I always walk to school. He is never late.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Position of frequency adverbs</strong></p>\n<p><strong>before the main verb · after am / is / are · between doesn't / don't and the verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We often visit our cousins. They are usually busy. He doesn't usually drive.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Habits and routines.</strong></p>\n<p>We use the present simple for things we do regularly.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I brush my teeth twice a day.</p>\n<p>▸ My father prays Fajr at the mosque every day.</p>\n<p>▸ We visit our grandparents on Fridays.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Facts and general truths.</strong></p>\n<p>We use it for things that are always or generally true.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Water boils at 100°C.</p>\n<p>▸ The sun rises in the east.</p>\n<p>▸ Camels live in the desert.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Timetables and schedules.</strong></p>\n<p>We use it for fixed times of transport, shops and events.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The train to Dammam leaves at 8:30.</p>\n<p>▸ The museum opens at nine and closes at five.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Likes, dislikes and states.</strong></p>\n<p>Verbs like like, love, want, know and need are normally in the simple form.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Huda loves science.</p>\n<p>▸ I don't know the answer.</p>\n<p>▸ Do you need help?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Spelling of -s: most verbs + s (works, plays) · -s, -sh, -ch, -x, -o + es (watches, goes, does) · consonant + y → -ies (studies, cries) · have → has.</p>\n<p>▸ Pronunciation: /s/ works · /z/ plays · /ɪz/ watches, washes.</p>\n<p>▸ Signal words: every day, every week, on Fridays, at weekends, in the morning, once a week, twice a month.</p>\n<p>▸ After does / doesn't the verb has NO -s: Does he play? (not Does he plays?)</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم المضارع البسيط للعادات والحقائق والجداول الزمنية. ويبقى الفعل في صورته الأصلية مع I وyou وwe وthey، ونضيف إليه s أو es مع he وshe وit أو الاسم المفرد.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في النفي نستخدم don't أو doesn't ثم الفعل في صورته الأصلية دون s، وفي السؤال نبدأ بـ Do أو Does ثم الفاعل ثم الفعل في صورته الأصلية. وفي أسئلة Wh- نضع أداة الاستفهام أولًا ثم do أو does.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ظروف التكرار مثل always وusually وnever تأتي قبل الفعل الرئيس، وبعد فعل be، فنقول I always walk وHe is always late.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He go to school by bus.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He goes to school by bus.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل مفرد غائب فنضيف es.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She doesn't likes coffee.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She doesn't like coffee.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد doesn't يأتي الفعل دون s.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Does he plays tennis?</em> <strong>→ ✓ Does he play tennis?</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد does يأتي الفعل في صورته الأصلية.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I am go to school every day.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I go to school every day.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نضع am قبل الفعل في المضارع البسيط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I eat always breakfast.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I always eat breakfast.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ظرف التكرار يأتي قبل الفعل الرئيس.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Where you live?</em> <strong>→ ✓ Where do you live?</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في السؤال نحتاج do أو does بعد أداة الاستفهام.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I / you / we / they work · he / she / it works</p>\n<p>don't work · doesn't work (never doesn't works)</p>\n<p>I always walk · I am always happy</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the subject: he / she / it or a singular noun → verb + -s / -es.</p>\n<p>2. After do, does, don't or doesn't, the verb is always the base form.</p>\n<p>3. Wh- questions need do / does unless Who or What is the subject.</p>\n<p>4. Frequency adverbs go before the main verb but after be; STEP often tests this position.</p>\n<p>5. Check -s spelling: studies, watches, goes, has.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد الفاعل أولًا، فإذا كان مفردًا غائبًا أضف s أو es، وبعد do وdoes يأتي الفعل دائمًا في صورته الأصلية، وضع ظرف التكرار قبل الفعل وبعد be.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. My father ______ to work at seven o'clock.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. go B. goes C. going D. is go</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The subject my father = he.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> he + verb + -es (go → goes).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفاعل مفرد غائب فنستخدم goes.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. What time ______ the shop open on Fridays?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. do B. is C. are D. does</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> This is a Wh- question with the main verb open.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The subject the shop is singular.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Singular subject → does. The answer is D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السؤال فيه فعل رئيس والفاعل مفرد فنستخدم does.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. On Mondays my (A) <u>brother</u> (B) <u>doesn't</u> (C) <u>plays</u> football (D) <u>with</u> us.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. brother B. doesn't C. plays D. with</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> After doesn't the verb must be the base form.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> plays should be play.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: On Mondays my brother doesn't play football with us. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد doesn't يأتي الفعل دون s.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 D · 3 C · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I ______ my teeth twice a day.","o":["brush","brushes","brushing","am brush"],"k":0,"e":"With I we use the base form: brush.","h":"مع I نستخدم الفعل في صورته الأصلية."},{"n":2,"s":"Hamad ______ in a bank in Dammam.","o":["work","working","works","is work"],"k":2,"e":"Hamad = he → works.","h":"الفاعل مفرد غائب فنضيف s."},{"n":3,"s":"We ______ English on Sundays and Tuesdays.","o":["studies","studying","studys","study"],"k":3,"e":"With we we use the base form: study.","h":"مع we نستخدم الصورة الأصلية."},{"n":4,"s":"My mother ______ the news in the evening.","o":["watchs","watch","watches","watching"],"k":2,"e":"Verbs ending in -ch add -es: watches.","h":"الفعل المنتهي بـ ch نضيف إليه es."},{"n":5,"s":"______ your sister speak French?","o":["Does","Do","Is","Are"],"k":0,"e":"Main verb speak + singular subject → Does.","h":"مع الفعل الرئيس والفاعل المفرد نستخدم Does."},{"n":6,"s":"They ______ live in Taif. They live in Abha.","o":["doesn't","don't","aren't","not"],"k":1,"e":"They + don't + base verb.","h":"مع they ننفي بـ don't."},{"n":7,"s":"My grandfather ______ a cup of coffee after lunch.","o":["have","has","haves","having"],"k":1,"e":"The he-form of have is has.","h":"صيغة have مع الغائب المفرد هي has."},{"n":8,"s":"Mona ______ like spicy food.","o":["don't","isn't","doesn't","not"],"k":2,"e":"Mona = she → doesn't + base verb.","h":"الفاعل مفرد مؤنث فننفي بـ doesn't."},{"n":9,"s":"I ______ walk to school because it is near my house.","o":["always","is always","am always","always to"],"k":0,"e":"The adverb comes before the main verb walk: I always walk.","h":"ظرف التكرار قبل الفعل الرئيس."},{"n":10,"s":"My little brother ______ his homework after dinner.","o":["do","dos","doing","does"],"k":3,"e":"do → does with he.","h":"الفعل do يصبح does مع الغائب."},{"n":11,"s":"Where ______ your cousins live?","o":["do","does","are","is"],"k":0,"e":"your cousins is plural → do.","h":"الفاعل جمع فنستخدم do."},{"n":12,"s":"The bus to the city centre ______ every twenty minutes.","o":["leave","leaving","is leave","leaves"],"k":3,"e":"The bus = it → leaves (timetable).","h":"الفاعل مفرد فنضيف s."},{"n":13,"s":"Salma is a good student. She is ______ late for class.","o":["ever","never","don't","doesn't"],"k":1,"e":"After is we put the adverb never: She is never late.","h":"بعد is نضع never."},{"n":14,"s":"\"______ does your brother go to the gym?\" \"Three times a week.\"","o":["How much","How many","How long","How often"],"k":3,"e":"Three times a week answers How often.","h":"السؤال عن عدد المرات يكون بـ How often."},{"n":15,"s":"My friends ______ football in the park on Fridays.","o":["play usually","usually plays","are usually play","usually play"],"k":3,"e":"The adverb goes before the verb, and friends takes play (no -s).","h":"الظرف قبل الفعل، والفاعل جمع فلا نضيف s."},{"n":16,"s":"\"Does your father drive to work?\" \"No, he ______. He takes the metro.\"","o":["doesn't","don't","isn't","not"],"k":0,"e":"The short answer to Does he …? is No, he doesn't.","h":"الإجابة القصيرة No, he doesn't."},{"n":17,"s":"Who ______ the cooking in your house?","o":["do","is","are","does"],"k":3,"e":"Who is the subject (singular), so the verb takes -es: does.","h":"Who هنا فاعل مفرد فنستخدم does."},{"n":18,"s":"Ali ______ hard for his exams every year.","o":["studys","study","studies","studyes"],"k":2,"e":"Consonant + y → -ies: studies.","h":"حرف ساكن + y يتحول إلى ies."},{"n":19,"s":"We don't ______ to school on Fridays.","o":["goes","going","went","go"],"k":3,"e":"After don't we use the base form go.","h":"بعد don't نستخدم الصورة الأصلية."},{"n":20,"s":"My brother never ______ meat; he doesn't like it.","o":["eat","eating","eats","doesn't eat"],"k":2,"e":"never already makes the sentence negative, so we use the positive form eats.","h":"never تفيد النفي فلا نضيف doesn't."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"My father (A) drink (B) coffee (C) every (D) morning.","o":["drink","coffee","every","morning"],"k":0,"e":"My father = he → drinks.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) Does your brother (B) plays tennis (C) at the (D) weekend?","o":["Does","plays","at","weekend"],"k":1,"e":"After Does the verb is the base form play.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"I (A) am go to school (B) by bus (C) with my (D) brother.","o":["am go","by","with","brother"],"k":0,"e":"The present simple does not use am before the verb.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"She doesn't (A) watch TV on school nights (B) because she (C) have homework (D) to do.","o":["watch","because","have","to"],"k":2,"e":"she takes has, not have.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"Where (A) does your uncle (B) works (C) in (D) Riyadh?","o":["does","works","in","Riyadh"],"k":1,"e":"After does the verb is the base form work.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"My cousins (A) sometimes (B) visits us, and they (C) always bring (D) sweets.","o":["sometimes","visits","always","sweets"],"k":1,"e":"My cousins is plural, so the verb is visit.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"Fahad (A) is (B) usually tired after school, so he (C) sleep for (D) an hour.","o":["is","usually","sleep","an"],"k":2,"e":"he → sleeps.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"We (A) go (B) never to the beach (C) in (D) summer; it is too hot.","o":["go","never","in","summer"],"k":1,"e":"never must come before the main verb go.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"My little sister (A) is four. She (B) sleeps a lot, and she (C) often (D) crys at night.","o":["is","sleeps","often","crys"],"k":3,"e":"Consonant + y → -ies: cries.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"How often (A) do your teacher (B) give you (C) a test? (D) Usually once a week.","o":["do","give","a","Usually"],"k":0,"e":"your teacher is singular, so we need does.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.6","t":"Present Continuous; Present Simple vs Present Continuous","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.6 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Form the present continuous (am / is / are + verb-ing) with correct -ing spelling.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the present simple or the present continuous from time signals (now, every day, at the moment).</p>\n<p>3. Recognize stative verbs that are not normally used in the continuous (know, like, want, need).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكوّن الطالب المضارع المستمر بصيغة am/is/are مع الفعل المنتهي بـ ing وبتهجئة صحيحة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار بين المضارع البسيط والمضارع المستمر حسب كلمات الزمن.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يتعرف أفعال الحالة التي لا تُستخدم عادةً في المستمر مثل know وlike وwant وneed.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Look! The baby ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. sleeps B. sleep C. is sleeping D. are sleeping</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. My father ______ to work every day.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. drives B. is driving C. drive D. driving</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. I ______ the answer to this question.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. am knowing B. know C. knowing D. knows</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Positive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>I + am + verb-ing · he / she / it + is + verb-ing · you / we / they + are + verb-ing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I am reading. She is cooking. They are playing.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + am not / isn't / aren't + verb-ing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He isn't sleeping. We aren't watching TV.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Questions and short answers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Am / Is / Are + subject + verb-ing …? — Yes, she is. / No, they aren't.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Are you listening? Yes, I am.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Wh- questions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Wh- word + am / is / are + subject + verb-ing …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. What are you doing? Where is Ali going?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Spelling: most verbs + ing</strong></p>\n<p><strong>read → reading · eat → eating · play → playing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The boys are playing outside.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Spelling: final -e → drop e + ing</strong></p>\n<p><strong>write → writing · make → making · come → coming</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She is writing an email.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Spelling: short vowel + one consonant → double</strong></p>\n<p><strong>sit → sitting · run → running · swim → swimming · stop → stopping</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The children are swimming in the pool.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Spelling: -ie → -ying</strong></p>\n<p><strong>lie → lying · die → dying · tie → tying</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The cat is lying on the sofa.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Actions happening now, at the moment of speaking.</strong></p>\n<p>We use the present continuous for something in progress right now.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Be quiet! The teacher is talking.</p>\n<p>▸ Mum is making lunch in the kitchen.</p>\n<p>▸ Look! It is raining in Abha.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Temporary actions around now.</strong></p>\n<p>We also use it for actions that continue for a short period, even if they are not happening at this exact second.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My brother is staying with us this week.</p>\n<p>▸ I am reading a great book these days.</p>\n<p>▸ We are studying for our exams this month.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Present simple = habits and facts; present continuous = now and temporary.</strong></p>\n<p>Compare a regular routine with what is happening at this moment.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Hessa usually walks to school, but today she is taking the bus.</p>\n<p>▸ My uncle works in Riyadh. This month he is working in Jeddah.</p>\n<p>▸ We eat dinner at eight. Right now we are eating a snack.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Stative verbs stay in the simple form.</strong></p>\n<p>Verbs of feelings, thinking and possession (like, love, hate, want, need, know, understand, believe, remember, own, belong) are normally not used with -ing.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I know your brother. (not I am knowing)</p>\n<p>▸ Do you understand the question?</p>\n<p>▸ This phone belongs to my sister.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Signal words for the present continuous: now, right now, at the moment, today, this week, these days, Look!, Listen!</p>\n<p>▸ Signal words for the present simple: every day, usually, always, often, never, on Fridays, at weekends.</p>\n<p>▸ have can be continuous when it means eat / drink / experience: We are having lunch. (but I have a car.)</p>\n<p>▸ Do not forget am / is / are: ✗ She cooking. ✓ She is cooking.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نكوّن المضارع المستمر من am أو is أو are ثم الفعل مضافًا إليه ing، ونستخدمه لحدث يقع الآن في لحظة الكلام، أو لحدث مؤقت يحدث في هذه الفترة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أما المضارع البسيط فنستخدمه للعادات والحقائق الثابتة. فإذا رأيت كلمات مثل now وat the moment وLook! فاختر المستمر، وإذا رأيت every day وusually وalways فاختر البسيط.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">هناك أفعال تسمى أفعال الحالة مثل know وlike وwant وneed وunderstand لا تُستخدم عادةً في المستمر، لأنها تصف حالة لا حدثًا.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She cooking now.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She is cooking now.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا بد من am أو is أو are قبل الفعل المنتهي بـ ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I am knowing the answer.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I know the answer.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">know فعل حالة لا يُستخدم في المستمر.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Look! The boys play football.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Look! The boys are playing football.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">كلمة Look! تدل على حدث يقع الآن فنستخدم المستمر.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He is go to school every day.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He goes to school every day.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع every day نستخدم المضارع البسيط دون is.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>They are swiming.</em> <strong>→ ✓ They are swimming.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نضاعف الحرف الأخير في swim قبل ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I am wanting some water.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I want some water.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">want فعل حالة يبقى في المضارع البسيط.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Present simple: I drink tea every morning. (habit)</p>\n<p>Present continuous: I am drinking tea now. (in progress)</p>\n<p>Stative: I like tea. (not I am liking tea)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Look for the time signal first: now / at the moment / Look! → continuous; every day / usually → simple.</p>\n<p>2. If the verb is a stative verb (know, want, like, need, belong), choose the simple form even with now.</p>\n<p>3. A continuous answer needs BOTH parts: am / is / are + verb-ing.</p>\n<p>4. Check -ing spelling: writing, sitting, lying — STEP error items love spelling mistakes.</p>\n<p>5. In error identification, a missing be (She cooking) or an extra be (He is go) is a classic trap.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث أولًا عن كلمة الزمن لتختار البسيط أو المستمر، وانتبه إلى أفعال الحالة التي تبقى في البسيط، وتأكد أن المستمر يتكون من am أو is أو are مع الفعل المنتهي بـ ing.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Please be quiet. The baby ______ in the next room.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. sleeps B. is sleeping C. sleep D. sleeping</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Please be quiet tells us the action is happening now.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Now → present continuous: is + sleeping.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحدث يقع الآن فنستخدم is sleeping.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. My cousin ______ three languages.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. is speaking B. are speaking C. speak D. speaks</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> This is a general fact about ability, not an action now.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Fact → present simple; my cousin = he → speaks.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة حقيقة ثابتة فنستخدم المضارع البسيط speaks.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. At the (A) <u>moment</u> my sister (B) <u>is</u> (C) <u>writeing</u> an email to (D) <u>her</u> teacher.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. moment B. is C. writeing D. her</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The structure is + verb-ing is correct.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> write ends in -e, so we drop the e: writing.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: At the moment my sister is writing an email to her teacher. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نحذف حرف e من write قبل إضافة ing.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 B · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Look! Those children ______ in the rain.","o":["play","are playing","is playing","plays"],"k":1,"e":"Look! shows an action happening now; children is plural → are playing.","h":"كلمة Look! تدل على الآن، والفاعل جمع."},{"n":2,"s":"I ______ my homework at the moment.","o":["am doing","do","is doing","doing"],"k":0,"e":"at the moment + I → am doing.","h":"مع at the moment والضمير I نستخدم am doing."},{"n":3,"s":"Faris ______ his bike to school every day.","o":["rides","is riding","ride","riding"],"k":0,"e":"every day is a habit → present simple: rides.","h":"every day عادة فنستخدم المضارع البسيط."},{"n":4,"s":"Listen! Someone ______ at the door.","o":["knocks","knock","is knocking","are knocking"],"k":2,"e":"Listen! shows an action now; someone is singular → is knocking.","h":"Listen! تدل على الآن والفاعل مفرد."},{"n":5,"s":"We ______ TV now. We are reading.","o":["aren't watching","don't watch","isn't watching","not watching"],"k":0,"e":"now + negative continuous with we → aren't watching.","h":"النفي في المستمر مع we يكون aren't."},{"n":6,"s":"My sister ______ chocolate. She eats it every day.","o":["is loving","love","loves","loving"],"k":2,"e":"love is a stative verb, so it stays in the simple form.","h":"love فعل حالة يبقى في البسيط."},{"n":7,"s":"\"What ______ you doing?\" \"I'm cleaning my room.\"","o":["do","is","am","are"],"k":3,"e":"The question is in the present continuous: What are you doing?","h":"السؤال في المستمر فنستخدم are مع you."},{"n":8,"s":"The water ______. Turn off the cooker, please.","o":["boils","is boiling","boil","are boiling"],"k":1,"e":"The action is happening now, so we use is boiling.","h":"الحدث يحدث الآن فنستخدم is boiling."},{"n":9,"s":"Ahmed is ______ in the swimming pool.","o":["swiming","swimming","swimmng","swims"],"k":1,"e":"swim: short vowel + one consonant → double the m: swimming.","h":"نضاعف الحرف الأخير في swim."},{"n":10,"s":"My father usually ______ at seven, but today he is starting at nine.","o":["starts","is starting","start","starting"],"k":0,"e":"usually shows a habit → present simple; father = he → starts.","h":"usually تدل على العادة فنستخدم البسيط."},{"n":11,"s":"\"Is Majed sleeping?\" \"No, he ______. He's reading.\"","o":["doesn't","aren't","isn't","not"],"k":2,"e":"The short answer to Is he …? is No, he isn't.","h":"الإجابة القصيرة No, he isn't."},{"n":12,"s":"I ______ what you mean. Can you say it again?","o":["am not understanding","not understand","don't understand","doesn't understand"],"k":2,"e":"understand is stative, so we use the simple negative: don't understand.","h":"understand فعل حالة فنستخدم البسيط."},{"n":13,"s":"This week my uncle ______ with us because his house is being painted.","o":["stays","stay","staying","is staying"],"k":3,"e":"A temporary situation (this week) → present continuous.","h":"حدث مؤقت هذا الأسبوع فنستخدم المستمر."},{"n":14,"s":"The cat is ______ on my bed again!","o":["lieing","lyeing","lying","lies"],"k":2,"e":"lie → lying (-ie changes to -y + ing).","h":"lie يصبح lying."},{"n":15,"s":"Why ______ Noura crying? Is she hurt?","o":["does","is","are","do"],"k":1,"e":"The question is about now and uses crying, so we need is.","h":"السؤال في المستمر والفاعل مفرد فنستخدم is."},{"n":16,"s":"These shoes ______ to my brother, not to me.","o":["are belonging","belongs","is belonging","belong"],"k":3,"e":"belong is stative; These shoes is plural → belong.","h":"belong فعل حالة والفاعل جمع."},{"n":17,"s":"Water ______ at 100 degrees Celsius.","o":["boils","is boiling","boil","are boiling"],"k":0,"e":"This is a scientific fact, so we use the present simple: boils.","h":"الحقائق العلمية تأتي في المضارع البسيط."},{"n":18,"s":"At the moment, more and more people ______ electric cars in Riyadh.","o":["buy","are buying","buys","is buying"],"k":1,"e":"at the moment + a changing situation → are buying (people is plural).","h":"موقف متغير الآن والفاعل جمع."},{"n":19,"s":"\"Do you need help?\" \"No, thanks. I ______ fine.\"","o":["do","does","am do","am doing"],"k":3,"e":"I'm doing fine describes how things are going now: am doing.","h":"نستخدم am doing لوصف الحال الآن."},{"n":20,"s":"We ______ lunch now, so I can't talk on the phone.","o":["have","has","are have","are having"],"k":3,"e":"have = eat here, so it can be continuous: are having.","h":"have بمعنى يأكل يمكن أن تأتي في المستمر."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Right (A) now the students (B) is (C) taking a test in (D) the hall.","o":["now","is","taking","the"],"k":1,"e":"the students is plural, so we need are.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"Be (A) quiet! The (B) baby (C) sleeping in (D) her room.","o":["quiet","baby","sleeping","her"],"k":2,"e":"The continuous needs is before sleeping.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"My brother (A) is go to (B) the gym (C) every (D) Monday.","o":["is go","the","every","Monday"],"k":0,"e":"every Monday is a habit, so we use the present simple goes.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"I (A) am knowing (B) many students (C) in (D) this school.","o":["am knowing","many","in","this"],"k":0,"e":"know is a stative verb and is not used in the continuous.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"Look! (A) The man (B) is (C) runing (D) after the bus.","o":["The","is","runing","after"],"k":2,"e":"run doubles the n: running.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"We (A) usually (B) eat dates after (C) lunch, but today we (D) eat fruit.","o":["usually","eat","lunch","eat"],"k":3,"e":"today shows a temporary change, so we need are eating.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"My mother (A) is (B) writing a (C) shoping list for (D) the supermarket.","o":["is","writing","shoping","the"],"k":2,"e":"shop doubles the p before -ing: shopping.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) Are you (B) wanting (C) some tea (D) with your breakfast?","o":["Are","wanting","some","with"],"k":1,"e":"want is stative, so the question is Do you want …?","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"These (A) days my (B) father (C) is (D) work from home.","o":["days","father","is","work"],"k":3,"e":"After is we need the -ing form working.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Listen! The birds (B) sing in the tree (C) outside (D) my window.","o":["Listen","sing","outside","my"],"k":1,"e":"Listen! shows an action now, so we need are singing.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.7","t":"Can / Can't, Imperatives and Would Like","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.7 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use can / can't for ability, permission and requests, always followed by the base form.</p>\n<p>2. Give instructions with positive and negative imperatives.</p>\n<p>3. Make polite offers and requests with would like + noun / to-infinitive.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب can وcan't للقدرة والإذن والطلب، مع الفعل في صورته الأصلية دائمًا.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يعطي تعليمات بصيغة الأمر المثبتة والمنفية.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يقدّم عروضًا وطلبات مهذبة باستخدام would like مع اسم أو مع to والفعل.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. My brother can ______ very fast.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. runs B. running C. to run D. run</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. ______ the window, please. It's hot.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Open B. Opens C. Opening D. To open</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. I would like ______ some water, please.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. have B. to have C. having D. has</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>can — positive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + can + base verb (same form for all subjects)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I can swim. She can speak English.</em></p>\n<p><strong>can — negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + can't (cannot) + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He can't drive. We cannot stay late.</em></p>\n<p><strong>can — questions and short answers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Can + subject + base verb …? — Yes, I can. / No, she can't.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Can you help me? Yes, I can.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Imperative — positive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Base verb + … (no subject)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Open your books. Sit down, please.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Imperative — negative</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Don't + base verb + …</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Don't run in the corridor. Don't forget your ID.</em></p>\n<p><strong>would like — noun</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + would like ('d like) + noun</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I'd like a cup of tea, please.</em></p>\n<p><strong>would like — verb</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + would like + to + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She would like to visit AlUla.</em></p>\n<p><strong>would like — offers and questions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Would you like + noun / to + verb …? — Yes, please. / No, thank you.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Would you like some dates? Yes, please.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. can for ability.</strong></p>\n<p>We use can / can't to say what someone is able or not able to do.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My grandfather can ride a camel.</p>\n<p>▸ Reem can't swim, but she can ride a bike.</p>\n<p>▸ Can your little brother read?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. can for permission and requests.</strong></p>\n<p>We use can to ask for or give permission, and to ask people to do things.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Can I use your pen, please?</p>\n<p>▸ You can sit here.</p>\n<p>▸ Can you open the door for me?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Imperatives for instructions, directions and warnings.</strong></p>\n<p>The imperative has no subject. We use it in classrooms, recipes, signs and directions.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Turn left at the mosque.</p>\n<p>▸ Mix the flour and the eggs.</p>\n<p>▸ Don't touch the oven. It's hot!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. would like for polite wants, offers and invitations.</strong></p>\n<p>would like is more polite than want. We use it in shops, restaurants and with guests.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I'd like a chicken sandwich, please.</p>\n<p>▸ Would you like to come to our house on Friday?</p>\n<p>▸ My parents would like to meet your teacher.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ can never takes -s and is never followed by to: ✗ She cans swim. ✗ I can to swim.</p>\n<p>▸ Pronunciation: can /kən/ is weak in positive sentences; can't /kɑːnt/ is strong.</p>\n<p>▸ Add please to make imperatives polite: Please close the door. / Close the door, please.</p>\n<p>▸ Answer Would you like …? with Yes, please / No, thank you — not Yes, I like.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم can للتعبير عن القدرة أو لطلب الإذن أو لطلب شيء من شخص آخر، ويأتي بعدها الفعل في صورته الأصلية دون to ودون s مع جميع الضمائر، ونفيها can't أو cannot.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">صيغة الأمر تبدأ بالفعل في صورته الأصلية دون فاعل، مثل Open the door، وفي النهي نضع Don't قبل الفعل، مثل Don't be late.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم would like للطلب أو العرض المهذب، ويأتي بعدها اسم مثل I'd like some tea، أو to مع الفعل مثل I'd like to go. وهي أكثر تهذيبًا من want.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She can speaks English.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She can speak English.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد can يأتي الفعل في صورته الأصلية دون s.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I can to swim.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I can swim.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نستخدم to بعد can.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>You don't run in the corridor! (as a rule)</em> <strong>→ ✓ Don't run in the corridor!</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النهي يبدأ بـ Don't دون فاعل.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I would like go home.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I would like to go home.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد would like نحتاج to قبل الفعل.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Would you like some juice? Yes, I like.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Yes, please.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الرد المهذب على العرض هو Yes, please.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Please you sit down.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Please sit down.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">صيغة الأمر لا تحتاج إلى فاعل.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>like = enjoy in general: I like coffee.</p>\n<p>would like = want now, politely: I'd like a coffee, please.</p>\n<p>can (ability) vs can (permission): I can swim. / Can I go out?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. After can / can't the verb is ALWAYS the base form — no -s, no to, no -ing.</p>\n<p>2. After would like the verb needs to: would like to visit.</p>\n<p>3. An imperative has no subject; a negative imperative starts with Don't.</p>\n<p>4. In dialogues, choose Yes, please / No, thank you after Would you like …?</p>\n<p>5. STEP error items often add -s after can or drop to after would like.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد can يأتي الفعل في صورته الأصلية دائمًا، وبعد would like نحتاج to قبل الفعل، وصيغة الأمر تبدأ بالفعل دون فاعل، والنهي يبدأ بـ Don't.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. My little sister can ______ to ten in English.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. counts B. to count C. count D. counting</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The modal can comes before the blank.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> After can we use the base form.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C (count).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد can يأتي الفعل في صورته الأصلية.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. \"Would you like some more rice?\" \"______\"</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Yes, please. B. Yes, I like. C. Yes, I would. D. Yes, I'd like.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> This is a polite offer.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The polite answer to an offer is Yes, please.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الرد المهذب على العرض هو Yes, please.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>Please</u> don't (B) <u>be</u> late, and (C) <u>to bring</u> your (D) <u>notebook</u> tomorrow.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Please B. be C. to bring D. notebook</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The sentence gives two instructions.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> An imperative uses the base verb with no to: bring.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: Please don't be late, and bring your notebook tomorrow. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">صيغة الأمر تبدأ بالفعل دون to.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 D · 2 A · 3 B · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I can ______ Arabic and English.","o":["speak","speaks","to speak","speaking"],"k":0,"e":"After can we use the base form: speak.","h":"بعد can الفعل في صورته الأصلية."},{"n":2,"s":"______ your hands before you eat.","o":["Washes","Wash","Washing","To wash"],"k":1,"e":"An instruction uses the imperative (base verb): Wash.","h":"صيغة الأمر تبدأ بالفعل الأصلي."},{"n":3,"s":"My grandmother ______ read without her glasses.","o":["don't","doesn't","isn't","can't"],"k":3,"e":"For ability we use can't + base verb.","h":"للقدرة المنفية نستخدم can't."},{"n":4,"s":"______ shout in the library, please.","o":["Not","No","Doesn't","Don't"],"k":3,"e":"A negative imperative starts with Don't.","h":"النهي يبدأ بـ Don't."},{"n":5,"s":"I'd like ______ orange juice, please.","o":["a","an","to","the"],"k":1,"e":"would like + noun; orange starts with a vowel sound → an orange juice.","h":"بعد would like اسم، وorange تبدأ بصوت متحرك."},{"n":6,"s":"\"Can you play the drums?\" \"No, I ______.\"","o":["don't","am not","cannot to","can't"],"k":3,"e":"The short answer to Can you …? is No, I can't.","h":"الإجابة القصيرة No, I can't."},{"n":7,"s":"______ I borrow your ruler, please?","o":["Can","Do","Am","Would like"],"k":0,"e":"To ask for permission we use Can I …?","h":"لطلب الإذن نستخدم Can I."},{"n":8,"s":"My parents would like ______ AlUla next spring.","o":["visit","visiting","to visit","visits"],"k":2,"e":"would like + to + base verb.","h":"بعد would like نستخدم to والفعل."},{"n":9,"s":"Hamad is very strong. He can ______ this heavy box easily.","o":["carry","carries","carrying","to carry"],"k":0,"e":"can + base verb: carry.","h":"بعد can الفعل الأصلي."},{"n":10,"s":"Please ______ your mobile phones during the exam.","o":["turns off","turning off","turn off","you turn off"],"k":2,"e":"After Please the imperative uses the base verb with no subject.","h":"بعد Please نستخدم الفعل الأصلي دون فاعل."},{"n":11,"s":"\"______ like a cup of tea?\" \"Yes, please.\"","o":["Do you","Would you","Are you","Can you"],"k":1,"e":"Yes, please answers an offer: Would you like …?","h":"Yes, please رد على عرض بـ Would you like."},{"n":12,"s":"______ the red button. It stops the machine.","o":["Not press","Don't presses","Don't press","No pressing"],"k":2,"e":"A negative imperative: Don't + base verb.","h":"النهي: Don't مع الفعل الأصلي."},{"n":13,"s":"Faisal can swim, but he ______ dive.","o":["doesn't can","can't to","can't","not can"],"k":2,"e":"The negative of can is can't + base verb.","h":"نفي can هو can't."},{"n":14,"s":"\"Would you like some dates?\" \"No, ______. I'm full.\"","o":["thank you","I wouldn't like","I don't","I can't"],"k":0,"e":"A polite refusal of an offer is No, thank you.","h":"الرفض المهذب No, thank you."},{"n":15,"s":"Excuse me. ______ you tell me the way to the station?","o":["Do","Are","Would like","Can"],"k":3,"e":"A polite request uses Can you …?","h":"للطلب المهذب نستخدم Can you."},{"n":16,"s":"Mix the sugar and the butter, and then ______ two eggs.","o":["add","adds","adding","to adding"],"k":0,"e":"A recipe uses imperatives: add.","h":"الوصفات تستخدم صيغة الأمر."},{"n":17,"s":"I'd like ______ my cousin in Madinah this weekend.","o":["call","calling","calls","to call"],"k":3,"e":"would like + to + base verb.","h":"بعد would like نستخدم to والفعل."},{"n":18,"s":"Children under ten ______ use the pool without an adult.","o":["don't can","can't","aren't","not can"],"k":1,"e":"A rule about permission: can't + base verb.","h":"قاعدة منع فنستخدم can't."},{"n":19,"s":"\"What would you like?\" \"______ the grilled fish, please.\"","o":["I like","I'm like","I'd like","I want to"],"k":2,"e":"A polite order in a restaurant: I'd like + noun.","h":"الطلب المهذب في المطعم I'd like."},{"n":20,"s":"______ worry about the test. You can do it!","o":["Don't","Not","Doesn't","No"],"k":0,"e":"A negative imperative to encourage: Don't worry.","h":"النهي بـ Don't."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"My (A) sister can (B) draws very (C) well with (D) pencils.","o":["sister","draws","well","pencils"],"k":1,"e":"After can we use the base form draw.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) You open your books (B) at page twenty, (C) please, and (D) read the story.","o":["You","at","please","read"],"k":0,"e":"An imperative has no subject, so You must be removed.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"I (A) would like (B) buy a (C) new bag (D) for school.","o":["would","buy","new","for"],"k":1,"e":"would like needs to before the verb: to buy.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"(A) Can you (B) to help me (C) with (D) this box?","o":["Can","to help","with","this"],"k":1,"e":"can is never followed by to.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) Not (B) park your car (C) in front of (D) the gate.","o":["Not","park","in front of","the"],"k":0,"e":"A negative imperative starts with Don't.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"Would you (A) like some (B) coffee? Yes, I (C) like, (D) thank you.","o":["like","coffee","like","thank"],"k":2,"e":"The answer to an offer is Yes, please, not Yes, I like.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"My uncle (A) can speak three (B) languages, and he (C) cans (D) write in two of them.","o":["can","languages","cans","write"],"k":2,"e":"can never takes -s.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) Please close (B) the door (C) when you (D) leaving.","o":["Please","the","when","leaving"],"k":3,"e":"After when you we need the present simple leave.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Can your brother (B) plays chess? Yes, he (C) can, and he (D) is very good.","o":["Can","plays","can","is"],"k":1,"e":"After can we use the base form play.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"Students (A) can't (B) use phones in class, so (C) don't (D) bringing them.","o":["can't","use","don't","bringing"],"k":3,"e":"After don't we use the base form bring.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.8","t":"Prepositions of Place and Time","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.8 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Choose in, on or at for times, days, dates and places.</p>\n<p>2. Describe location with under, next to, between, behind, in front of and opposite.</p>\n<p>3. Use before and after with nouns, times and events.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يختار الطالب in أو on أو at مع الأوقات والأيام والتواريخ والأماكن.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يصف الأماكن باستخدام under وnext to وbetween وbehind وin front of وopposite.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم before وafter مع الأسماء والأوقات والمناسبات.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. My birthday is ______ May.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. on B. at C. in D. to</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. The cat is sleeping ______ the table.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. under B. at C. in front D. on to</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. The lesson starts ______ eight o'clock.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. in B. on C. to D. at</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Time: at</strong></p>\n<p><strong>at + clock time · at night · at noon · at the weekend (BrE)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The bus leaves at 6:45. I study at night.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Time: on</strong></p>\n<p><strong>on + day · on + date · on + special day</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. on Sunday · on 23 September · on National Day · on my birthday</em></p>\n<p><strong>Time: in</strong></p>\n<p><strong>in + month · in + year · in + season · in the morning / afternoon / evening</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. in March · in 2030 · in winter · in the evening</em></p>\n<p><strong>Place: at</strong></p>\n<p><strong>at + a point or an address · at school · at home · at work · at the door</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. My father is at work. Someone is at the door.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Place: on</strong></p>\n<p><strong>on + a surface · on the wall · on the floor · on the second floor · on the bus</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The map is on the wall.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Place: in</strong></p>\n<p><strong>in + an enclosed space · in a room · in a box · in Riyadh · in Saudi Arabia</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The keys are in my bag.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Position</strong></p>\n<p><strong>under · next to · between A and B · behind · in front of · opposite · near · above</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The pharmacy is between the bank and the bakery.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Sequence</strong></p>\n<p><strong>before / after + noun or time</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Wash your hands before lunch. We play after school.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Times and dates.</strong></p>\n<p>Think from small to big: at for an exact time, on for a day or date, in for longer periods.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The match starts at 9 p.m.</p>\n<p>▸ We visit Grandma on Fridays.</p>\n<p>▸ School finishes in June.</p>\n<p>▸ It is very hot in summer.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Places: points, surfaces and enclosed spaces.</strong></p>\n<p>at for a point or place where an activity happens, on for a surface, in for inside something or a city / country.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Meet me at the gate.</p>\n<p>▸ Your phone is on the desk.</p>\n<p>▸ My cousins live in Dammam.</p>\n<p>▸ The milk is in the fridge.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Describing position.</strong></p>\n<p>Use position words to show exactly where things are.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The shoes are under the bed.</p>\n<p>▸ Sit next to Omar.</p>\n<p>▸ The post office is opposite the park.</p>\n<p>▸ There is a tall tree behind our house.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. before and after.</strong></p>\n<p>They show which event comes first.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Brush your teeth before bed.</p>\n<p>▸ We have a break after the second lesson.</p>\n<p>▸ Call me after 5 o'clock.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ No preposition before this / next / last / every / tomorrow / yesterday: We travel next week. (not in next week)</p>\n<p>▸ in the morning, but at night; on Monday morning (a specific day).</p>\n<p>▸ between is for two things; among is for more than two.</p>\n<p>▸ in front of = before something (facing it); opposite = on the other side, facing it.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم at مع الساعة والوقت المحدد، وon مع الأيام والتواريخ، وin مع الشهور والسنوات والفصول وأجزاء اليوم مثل in the morning، ونقول at night.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في المكان نستخدم at مع النقطة أو المكان الذي يُمارس فيه نشاط مثل at school، وon مع السطح مثل on the wall، وin مع الداخل والمدن والدول مثل in the box وin Riyadh.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نستخدم حرف جر قبل next وlast وthis وevery وtomorrow، فنقول next week لا in next week. وكلمة between تكون بين شيئين.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>in Sunday</em> <strong>→ ✓ on Sunday</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأيام تأخذ on.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>at 2025</em> <strong>→ ✓ in 2025</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السنوات تأخذ in.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>in the night</em> <strong>→ ✓ at night</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نقول at night بخلاف in the morning.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I will travel in next week.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I will travel next week.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا حرف جر قبل next.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The book is on the bag. (inside)</em> <strong>→ ✓ The book is in the bag.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للداخل نستخدم in.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>between the bank with the café</em> <strong>→ ✓ between the bank and the café</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">between تأتي مع and.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>at 7:00 → on Monday → in March → in 2026 (small → big)</p>\n<p>at the station (a point) · on the platform (a surface) · in the train (inside)</p>\n<p>in front of the car (facing its front) · opposite the café (across the street) · behind the school (at the back)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the noun after the blank: clock time → at; day / date → on; month / year / season → in.</p>\n<p>2. For places, picture it: a point → at, a surface → on, inside → in.</p>\n<p>3. Watch for next / last / every / this — they need no preposition.</p>\n<p>4. between always goes with and; check the second noun.</p>\n<p>5. STEP error items often swap in / on / at in dates and places.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">انظر إلى الاسم بعد الفراغ: الساعة مع at، واليوم والتاريخ مع on، والشهر والسنة والفصل مع in، وتخيّل المكان: نقطة أم سطح أم داخل.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Our school trip is ______ Thursday morning.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. in B. on C. at D. to</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The time phrase is Thursday morning.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> A specific day (even with morning) takes on.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع يوم محدد نستخدم on حتى لو جاءت بعده كلمة morning.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The pharmacy is ______ the bank and the bakery.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. next B. under C. behind D. between</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> We see two places joined by and.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Position in the middle of two things → between.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بين شيئين مع and نستخدم between.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. We (A) <u>always</u> have (B) <u>a</u> long holiday (C) <u>on</u> summer (D) <u>with</u> our family.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. always B. a C. on D. with</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> summer is a season.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Seasons take in, not on.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: We always have a long holiday in summer with our family. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفصول تأخذ in.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 D · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I wake up ______ six o'clock every day.","o":["in","on","to","at"],"k":3,"e":"Clock times take at.","h":"الساعة تأخذ at."},{"n":2,"s":"We don't go to school ______ Friday.","o":["in","on","at","to"],"k":1,"e":"Days take on.","h":"الأيام تأخذ on."},{"n":3,"s":"Ramadan is ______ March this year.","o":["on","at","to","in"],"k":3,"e":"Months take in.","h":"الشهور تأخذ in."},{"n":4,"s":"Your shoes are ______ the bed. Look down!","o":["on","above","at","under"],"k":3,"e":"Look down! tells us they are under the bed.","h":"Look down! تعني أنها تحت السرير."},{"n":5,"s":"My father is ______ work now. He comes home at four.","o":["in","on","at","to"],"k":2,"e":"We say at work.","h":"نقول at work."},{"n":6,"s":"The picture is ______ the wall in the living room.","o":["on","in","at","under"],"k":0,"e":"A wall is a surface → on.","h":"الحائط سطح فنستخدم on."},{"n":7,"s":"My cousins live ______ Jeddah.","o":["at","in","on","to"],"k":1,"e":"Cities take in.","h":"المدن تأخذ in."},{"n":8,"s":"I usually read ______ night before I sleep.","o":["at","in","on","to"],"k":0,"e":"We say at night.","h":"نقول at night."},{"n":9,"s":"The milk is ______ the fridge.","o":["in","on","at","under"],"k":0,"e":"Inside the fridge → in.","h":"داخل الثلاجة in."},{"n":10,"s":"Please sit ______ Khalid. There is an empty chair beside him.","o":["between","next to","under","opposite of"],"k":1,"e":"beside him = next to him.","h":"بجانبه = next to."},{"n":11,"s":"My sister was born ______ 2012.","o":["on","at","since","in"],"k":3,"e":"Years take in.","h":"السنوات تأخذ in."},{"n":12,"s":"We usually go for a walk ______ the evening.","o":["at","on","to","in"],"k":3,"e":"We say in the evening.","h":"نقول in the evening."},{"n":13,"s":"Saudi National Day is ______ 23 September.","o":["on","in","at","to"],"k":0,"e":"Dates take on.","h":"التواريخ تأخذ on."},{"n":14,"s":"The bus stop is ______ our school, on the other side of the street.","o":["between","under","opposite","behind"],"k":2,"e":"On the other side of the street, facing it = opposite.","h":"في الجهة المقابلة = opposite."},{"n":15,"s":"Wash the fruit ______ you eat it.","o":["before","after","between","until"],"k":0,"e":"Washing comes first, so we use before.","h":"الغسل يكون قبل الأكل."},{"n":16,"s":"We are going to visit our grandparents ______ weekend.","o":["next","in next","on next","at next"],"k":0,"e":"No preposition before next.","h":"لا حرف جر قبل next."},{"n":17,"s":"The car park is ______ the hospital, at the back of the building.","o":["in front of","opposite","behind","on"],"k":2,"e":"at the back of = behind.","h":"في الخلف = behind."},{"n":18,"s":"My uncle works ______ the third floor of that building.","o":["in","on","at","to"],"k":1,"e":"Floors take on.","h":"الطوابق تأخذ on."},{"n":19,"s":"We have a short break ______ the second and third lessons.","o":["among","in","at","between"],"k":3,"e":"Two things (second and third lessons) → between.","h":"بين شيئين between."},{"n":20,"s":"The museum is closed ______ Tuesday mornings.","o":["in","at","during the","on"],"k":3,"e":"A day + morning still takes on.","h":"اليوم مع morning يأخذ on."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"My exam is (A) on Sunday (B) at nine o'clock (C) on (D) the morning.","o":["on","at","on","the"],"k":2,"e":"We say in the morning.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"We (A) live (B) at Riyadh, (C) near the (D) new metro station.","o":["live","at","near","new"],"k":1,"e":"Cities take in.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"The (A) keys are (B) on the table, next (C) of the (D) lamp.","o":["keys","on","of","lamp"],"k":2,"e":"The correct phrase is next to.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"I (A) always visit (B) my grandmother (C) in (D) Fridays.","o":["always","my","in","Fridays"],"k":2,"e":"Days take on.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"My family (A) moved to Taif (B) in 2019, and we (C) still live there (D) at now.","o":["moved","in","still","at now"],"k":3,"e":"now needs no preposition.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"The (A) cat is sleeping (B) between the sofa (C) or the (D) chair.","o":["cat","between","or","chair"],"k":2,"e":"between goes with and, not or.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"Let's (A) meet (B) in the main gate (C) after (D) school.","o":["meet","in","after","school"],"k":1,"e":"A meeting point takes at: at the gate.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"We (A) are (B) travelling to Abha (C) in (D) next month.","o":["are","travelling","in","next"],"k":2,"e":"next month needs no preposition.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) At winter it is (B) very cold (C) at night (D) in the desert.","o":["At","very","at","in"],"k":0,"e":"Seasons take in.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"Please (A) wait for me (B) in front the bank (C) on King Fahd Road (D) after lunch.","o":["wait","in front","on","after"],"k":1,"e":"The full phrase is in front of.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.9","t":"Basic Conjunctions and Word Order (and, but, or, because, so)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.9 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Join two ideas with and, but, or, because or so according to meaning.</p>\n<p>2. Build sentences in the order Subject + Verb + Object + Place + Time.</p>\n<p>3. Detect word-order errors such as a car red or I like very much football.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يربط الطالب بين فكرتين باستخدام and أو but أو or أو because أو so حسب المعنى.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يبني الجملة بالترتيب: الفاعل ثم الفعل ثم المفعول ثم المكان ثم الزمان.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يكتشف أخطاء ترتيب الكلمات مثل a car red وI like very much football.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. I like tea, ______ I don't like coffee.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. and B. or C. but D. so</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. It was raining, ______ we stayed at home.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. so B. because C. or D. but</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. My brother has ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. a car red B. red a car C. a red car D. car a red</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>and = addition</strong></p>\n<p><strong>idea 1 + and + idea 2 (same direction)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I play football and my brother plays tennis.</em></p>\n<p><strong>but = contrast</strong></p>\n<p><strong>idea 1 + , but + opposite idea</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The phone is nice, but it is expensive.</em></p>\n<p><strong>or = choice</strong></p>\n<p><strong>option 1 + or + option 2</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Do you want juice or water?</em></p>\n<p><strong>because = reason</strong></p>\n<p><strong>result + because + reason</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I am tired because I didn't sleep well.</em></p>\n<p><strong>so = result</strong></p>\n<p><strong>reason + , so + result</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I didn't sleep well, so I am tired.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Basic word order</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + Verb + Object + Place + Time</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Ali played football in the park yesterday.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adjective position</strong></p>\n<p><strong>adjective + noun · be + adjective</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. a big house · The house is big.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Adverb position (very much / well)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Verb + Object + very much / well</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I like football very much. She speaks English well.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. and joins similar ideas.</strong></p>\n<p>We use and to add information.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My mother is a teacher and my father is an engineer.</p>\n<p>▸ We bought dates and coffee.</p>\n<p>▸ Salem can swim and dive.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. but shows a contrast.</strong></p>\n<p>We use but when the second idea is different or surprising.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Taif is cool in summer, but Riyadh is very hot.</p>\n<p>▸ I studied hard, but the test was difficult.</p>\n<p>▸ He is young, but he is very wise.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. or gives a choice.</strong></p>\n<p>We use or in questions and in negative sentences.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Would you like tea or coffee?</p>\n<p>▸ We can go by bus or by car.</p>\n<p>▸ I don't eat meat or fish.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. because gives a reason; so gives a result.</strong></p>\n<p>because answers Why?; so tells us what happened next.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ We stayed inside because it was very windy.</p>\n<p>▸ It was very windy, so we stayed inside.</p>\n<p>▸ She is happy because she passed her exam.</p>\n<p>▸ She passed her exam, so she is happy.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>5. Word order: S + V + O + Place + Time.</strong></p>\n<p>English word order is fixed. Place comes before time, and adjectives come before nouns.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My cousin visited us in Jeddah last week.</p>\n<p>▸ I bought a new phone yesterday.</p>\n<p>▸ We eat dinner at home every evening.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Put a comma before but and so when they join two full sentences: It was late, so we went home.</p>\n<p>▸ Do not use because and so together: ✗ Because I was ill, so I stayed home.</p>\n<p>▸ Do not put very much between the verb and the object: ✗ I like very much tea. ✓ I like tea very much.</p>\n<p>▸ Place before time: ✓ I go to the gym on Mondays. (not on Mondays to the gym after the verb)</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم and للإضافة، وbut للمقابلة أو التعارض، وor للاختيار، وbecause لذكر السبب، وso لذكر النتيجة. ولا نجمع because وso في جملة واحدة كما يحدث أحيانًا في العربية مع «لأن … لذلك».</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ترتيب الجملة الإنجليزية ثابت: الفاعل ثم الفعل ثم المفعول ثم المكان ثم الزمان، مثل Ali played football in the park yesterday.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الصفة في الإنجليزية تأتي قبل الاسم، بخلاف العربية، فنقول a red car لا a car red، ونضع very much بعد المفعول لا قبله.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>a car red</em> <strong>→ ✓ a red car</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الصفة تأتي قبل الاسم في الإنجليزية.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I like very much football.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I like football very much.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">very much تأتي بعد المفعول.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Because it was hot, so we swam.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Because it was hot, we swam.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نجمع because وso معًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He is tired but he worked all day.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He is tired because he worked all day.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">العلاقة هنا سبب لا تعارض.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Yesterday I went to the market in the morning yesterday.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I went to the market yesterday morning.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نكرر الزمن، ونضعه في نهاية الجملة غالبًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I go every day to school.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I go to school every day.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المكان قبل الزمان.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>because + reason: I stayed home because I was sick.</p>\n<p>so + result: I was sick, so I stayed home.</p>\n<p>but + contrast: I was sick, but I went to school.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Ask: Is the second idea a reason (because), a result (so), a contrast (but), a choice (or) or extra information (and)?</p>\n<p>2. Read both halves of the sentence before choosing the linker.</p>\n<p>3. For word-order items, check: adjective before noun, object before very much, place before time.</p>\n<p>4. A sentence cannot have both because and so for the same idea.</p>\n<p>5. STEP options often include all five linkers — eliminate by meaning, not by grammar.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجملة كلها ثم حدّد العلاقة بين الفكرتين: إضافة أم تعارض أم اختيار أم سبب أم نتيجة، وفي أسئلة الترتيب تذكّر أن الصفة قبل الاسم والمكان قبل الزمان.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The museum was closed, ______ we went to the park instead.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. because B. or C. so D. but</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Idea 1: the museum was closed. Idea 2: we went to the park.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Idea 2 is the result of idea 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Result → so. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفكرة الثانية نتيجة للأولى فنستخدم so.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. My uncle bought ______ last month.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. a car white new B. a new white car</p>\n<p>C. a white new car D. new a white car</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Adjectives come before the noun.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Opinion / age (new) usually comes before colour (white).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> a new white car. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الصفات قبل الاسم، وصفة العمر new قبل اللون white.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>My</u> sister (B) <u>likes</u> (C) <u>very much</u> reading (D) <u>stories</u> in English.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. My B. likes C. very much D. stories</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> very much is between the verb likes and the object reading.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> very much must come after the object.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: My sister likes reading stories in English very much. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">very much تأتي بعد المفعول لا قبله.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 C · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I have a brother ______ a sister.","o":["and","but","or","so"],"k":0,"e":"Adding information → and.","h":"الإضافة تكون بـ and."},{"n":2,"s":"Do you want rice ______ bread with your chicken?","o":["and","so","or","because"],"k":2,"e":"A choice in a question → or.","h":"الاختيار بـ or."},{"n":3,"s":"I like football, ______ my sister likes basketball.","o":["so","but","because","or"],"k":1,"e":"Two different preferences → but.","h":"التعارض بـ but."},{"n":4,"s":"We took umbrellas ______ it was raining.","o":["so","but","or","because"],"k":3,"e":"it was raining is the reason → because.","h":"السبب بـ because."},{"n":5,"s":"It was very hot, ______ we went to the swimming pool.","o":["because","so","or","but"],"k":1,"e":"going to the pool is the result → so.","h":"النتيجة بـ so."},{"n":6,"s":"My father drives ______.","o":["a car big black","big a black car","a big black car","a black car big"],"k":2,"e":"Adjectives come before the noun: a big black car.","h":"الصفات قبل الاسم."},{"n":7,"s":"I play tennis ______.","o":["every Saturday","Saturday every","every on Saturday","in every Saturday"],"k":0,"e":"every + day, with no preposition.","h":"every مع اليوم دون حرف جر."},{"n":8,"s":"She is tired ______ she worked all day.","o":["because","so","but","or"],"k":0,"e":"worked all day is the reason → because.","h":"السبب بـ because."},{"n":9,"s":"He studied hard, ______ he passed the test easily.","o":["because","but","or","so"],"k":3,"e":"passing the test is the result → so.","h":"النتيجة بـ so."},{"n":10,"s":"My grandfather is old, ______ he is very active.","o":["so","because","but","and so"],"k":2,"e":"old vs very active is a surprising contrast → but.","h":"التعارض المفاجئ بـ but."},{"n":11,"s":"We can go to the mall by taxi ______ by metro.","o":["but","so","because","or"],"k":3,"e":"Two choices → or.","h":"خياران بـ or."},{"n":12,"s":"Turki speaks English ______.","o":["very good","very well","well very","very much well"],"k":1,"e":"The adverb well describes speaks and goes after the object.","h":"الظرف well بعد المفعول."},{"n":13,"s":"I don't drink coffee ______ tea in the evening.","o":["or","and","but","so"],"k":0,"e":"In negative sentences we join choices with or.","h":"في النفي نربط بـ or."},{"n":14,"s":"Our neighbours ______ last night.","o":["at home visited us","visited us at home","visited at home us","us visited at home"],"k":1,"e":"Order: Verb + Object + Place + Time.","h":"الترتيب: الفعل ثم المفعول ثم المكان ثم الزمان."},{"n":15,"s":"I love this city ______ the people are very kind.","o":["so","or","because","but"],"k":2,"e":"the people are kind is the reason I love the city → because.","h":"السبب بـ because."},{"n":16,"s":"The shop was closed, ______ we came back the next day.","o":["but","so","because","or"],"k":1,"e":"Coming back the next day is the result → so.","h":"النتيجة بـ so."},{"n":17,"s":"Fatimah enjoys ______.","o":["science lessons very much","very much science lessons","science very much lessons","very science lessons much"],"k":0,"e":"very much goes after the object.","h":"very much بعد المفعول."},{"n":18,"s":"The test was short, ______ it was not easy.","o":["so","because","or","but"],"k":3,"e":"short vs not easy is a contrast → but.","h":"التعارض بـ but."},{"n":19,"s":"We bought ______ for the living room.","o":["two chairs comfortable","comfortable two chairs","two comfortable chairs","chairs two comfortable"],"k":2,"e":"Number + adjective + noun: two comfortable chairs.","h":"العدد ثم الصفة ثم الاسم."},{"n":20,"s":"Because the road was busy, ______.","o":["so we arrived late","but we arrived late","we arrived late","or we arrived late"],"k":2,"e":"A sentence with because does not also need so.","h":"لا نجمع because وso."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"We have (A) a cat white and (B) two small (C) birds at (D) home.","o":["a cat white","two","birds","home"],"k":0,"e":"The adjective must come before the noun: a white cat.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"I wanted to go out, (A) but my (B) mother said it (C) was too late, (D) because I stayed home.","o":["but","mother","was","because"],"k":3,"e":"Staying home is the result, so we need so.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"Do you (A) prefer the blue shirt (B) and the green (C) one for (D) the party?","o":["prefer","and","one","the"],"k":1,"e":"A choice between two things needs or.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"Huda (A) is very (B) happy (C) so she (D) won the competition.","o":["is","happy","so","won"],"k":2,"e":"Winning is the reason for being happy, so we need because.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) I like very much chocolate, (B) but I (C) don't eat it (D) often.","o":["I like very much","but","don't","often"],"k":0,"e":"very much must come after the object chocolate.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"My cousin (A) speaks English (B) and French (C) very (D) good.","o":["speaks","and","very","good"],"k":3,"e":"To describe a verb we need the adverb well, not the adjective good.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"We (A) visited our (B) grandparents (C) last week in Taif and (D) stayed two days.","o":["visited","grandparents","last week in Taif","stayed"],"k":2,"e":"Place comes before time: in Taif last week.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"I (A) was hungry, (B) or I (C) made a (D) sandwich.","o":["was","or","made","sandwich"],"k":1,"e":"Making a sandwich is the result of being hungry → so.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"We (A) stayed in (B) a hotel (C) near the (D) beach beautiful.","o":["stayed","a","near","beach beautiful"],"k":3,"e":"The adjective must come before the noun: the beautiful beach.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Football I like, (B) but my brother (C) prefers (D) tennis.","o":["Football I like","but","prefers","tennis"],"k":0,"e":"English word order is Subject + Verb + Object: I like football.","h":""}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions. Questions 1–35: choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence. Questions 36–50: choose the ONE underlined part that is incorrect.","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا؛ في الأسئلة من ١ إلى ٣٥ اختر الإجابة التي تكمل الجملة، وفي الأسئلة من ٣٦ إلى ٥٠ اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–35)"],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"My best friend ______ from Taif.","o":["are","am","is","be"],"k":2,"e":"My best friend is singular → is.","h":"الفاعل مفرد فيأخذ is."},{"n":2,"s":"Can you help ______ with my homework?","o":["I","my","me","mine"],"k":2,"e":"After help we use the object pronoun me.","h":"بعد الفعل نستخدم me."},{"n":3,"s":"My uncle is ______ airline pilot.","o":["a","two","some","an"],"k":3,"e":"airline starts with a vowel sound → an.","h":"airline تبدأ بصوت متحرك."},{"n":4,"s":"There are three ______ in our street.","o":["bakerys","bakery","bakeries","bakeryes"],"k":2,"e":"Consonant + y → -ies: bakeries.","h":"حرف ساكن + y يصبح ies."},{"n":5,"s":"Is ______ your sister's phone on the sofa?","o":["this","these","those","they"],"k":0,"e":"One phone → this.","h":"مفرد فنستخدم this."},{"n":6,"s":"There ______ a new library in our town.","o":["are","have","is","has"],"k":2,"e":"a new library is singular → There is.","h":"الاسم مفرد فنستخدم There is."},{"n":7,"s":"My cousin ______ in a hospital in Abha.","o":["work","working","works","is work"],"k":2,"e":"My cousin = he → works.","h":"الفاعل مفرد غائب."},{"n":8,"s":"Look! The plane ______ off now.","o":["takes","take","taking","is taking"],"k":3,"e":"Look! and now → present continuous.","h":"Look! تدل على الآن."},{"n":9,"s":"I can ______ a bike, but I can't drive a car.","o":["ride","rides","riding","to ride"],"k":0,"e":"can + base verb.","h":"بعد can الفعل الأصلي."},{"n":10,"s":"We have English ______ Monday and Wednesday.","o":["in","at","to","on"],"k":3,"e":"Days take on.","h":"الأيام تأخذ on."},{"n":11,"s":"I was hungry, ______ I ate a sandwich.","o":["because","so","but","or"],"k":1,"e":"Eating is the result → so.","h":"النتيجة بـ so."},{"n":12,"s":"Mr. Saleh and his wife ______ our new neighbours.","o":["are","is","am","be"],"k":0,"e":"Two people joined by and → are.","h":"فاعل مركب جمع."},{"n":13,"s":"Please give me two ______ of bread.","o":["loafs","loaves","loaf","loafes"],"k":1,"e":"loaf → loaves.","h":"loaf يصبح loaves."},{"n":14,"s":"The boys are washing ______ hands.","o":["there","his","they","their"],"k":3,"e":"The owners are the boys → their.","h":"المالكون جمع."},{"n":15,"s":"My grandparents ______ got a farm near Al-Kharj.","o":["has","is","are","have"],"k":3,"e":"My grandparents = they → have got.","h":"الفاعل جمع."},{"n":16,"s":"______ your brother go to the same school as you?","o":["Do","Does","Is","Are"],"k":1,"e":"your brother + main verb go → Does.","h":"فاعل مفرد مع فعل رئيس."},{"n":17,"s":"Please don't make noise. Grandfather ______ a rest.","o":["has","have","having","is having"],"k":3,"e":"have = take a rest is happening now → is having.","h":"الحدث الآن."},{"n":18,"s":"______ the green line on the map to find the station.","o":["Follows","Following","Follow","You following"],"k":2,"e":"An instruction → imperative.","h":"صيغة الأمر."},{"n":19,"s":"The children's playground is ______ the mosque and the school.","o":["among","next","opposite to","between"],"k":3,"e":"Two places joined by and → between.","h":"بين شيئين."},{"n":20,"s":"We stayed at home ______ there was a dust storm.","o":["so","but","or","because"],"k":3,"e":"The dust storm is the reason → because.","h":"السبب بـ because."},{"n":21,"s":"My sister's room is tidy, but ______ is messy.","o":["my","mine","me","I"],"k":1,"e":"We need a word that stands alone without a noun: mine.","h":"نحتاج ضميرًا يقوم مقام الاسم."},{"n":22,"s":"There isn't ______ furniture in the new flat yet.","o":["any","many","a","some of"],"k":0,"e":"furniture is uncountable; negative → any.","h":"غير معدود في النفي."},{"n":23,"s":"\"Have you got any brothers?\" \"No, I ______.\"","o":["don't","haven't got any","am not","haven't"],"k":3,"e":"Short answer: No, I haven't.","h":"الإجابة القصيرة No, I haven't."},{"n":24,"s":"My father rarely ______ coffee at night.","o":["drink","drinks","is drinking","drinking"],"k":1,"e":"Frequency adverb + present simple; he → drinks.","h":"ظرف تكرار مع المضارع البسيط."},{"n":25,"s":"\"Why are you smiling?\" \"Because I ______ about the trip tomorrow.\"","o":["think","thinks","am thinking","thinking"],"k":2,"e":"think = plan in mind now → am thinking.","h":"حدث ذهني الآن."},{"n":26,"s":"\"Would you like ______ with us?\" \"Yes, please.\"","o":["to come","come","coming","comes"],"k":0,"e":"would like + to + verb.","h":"بعد would like نستخدم to."},{"n":27,"s":"The final match is ______ 8 p.m. ______ Thursday.","o":["on / at","at / on","in / on","at / in"],"k":1,"e":"Clock time → at; day → on.","h":"الساعة at واليوم on."},{"n":28,"s":"Badr is good at maths, ______ he finds English difficult.","o":["but","so","because","and so"],"k":0,"e":"good at maths vs English difficult → contrast.","h":"تعارض بـ but."},{"n":29,"s":"Our teacher gave ______ students a short quiz.","o":["she","hers","her","herself"],"k":2,"e":"Before the noun students we need the possessive her.","h":"قبل الاسم صفة ملكية."},{"n":30,"s":"______ Fahad and his brother at the mosque now?","o":["Is","Are","Do","Does"],"k":1,"e":"Fahad and his brother is plural; no main verb → Are.","h":"فاعل جمع دون فعل رئيس."},{"n":31,"s":"There ______ two good reasons to arrive early.","o":["is","has","are","have"],"k":2,"e":"two good reasons is plural → There are.","h":"الاسم جمع."},{"n":32,"s":"What time ______ the shops close on Thursdays?","o":["do","does","are","is"],"k":0,"e":"the shops is plural → do.","h":"الفاعل جمع."},{"n":33,"s":"I ______ this word. What does it mean?","o":["don't know","am not knowing","not know","doesn't know"],"k":0,"e":"know is stative → simple negative.","h":"know فعل حالة."},{"n":34,"s":"Visitors ______ take photos inside the museum. It is not allowed.","o":["don't can","can't to","can't","not can"],"k":2,"e":"Not allowed → can't + base verb.","h":"المنع بـ can't."},{"n":35,"s":"We will meet ______ the entrance ______ ten minutes before the show.","o":["at / —","in / at","on / in","at / in"],"k":0,"e":"A meeting point → at; ten minutes before needs no preposition.","h":"نقطة اللقاء at، ولا حرف جر قبل ten minutes before."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 36–50)"],"q":[{"n":36,"s":"(A) Ali and (B) me (C) are in the (D) school team.","o":["Ali","me","are","school"],"k":1,"e":"The pronoun is part of the subject → I.","h":""},{"n":37,"s":"I need (A) two (B) pieces of (C) paper and some (D) informations.","o":["two","pieces","paper","informations"],"k":3,"e":"information is uncountable.","h":""},{"n":38,"s":"(A) Its very (B) cold today, so (C) wear your (D) coat.","o":["Its","cold","wear","coat"],"k":0,"e":"It is → It's (with an apostrophe).","h":""},{"n":39,"s":"There (A) are a lot of (B) sand (C) in my (D) shoes.","o":["are","sand","in","shoes"],"k":0,"e":"sand is uncountable → There is.","h":""},{"n":40,"s":"(A) Can I (B) to use your (C) pencil for a (D) minute?","o":["Can","to use","pencil","minute"],"k":1,"e":"No to after can.","h":""},{"n":41,"s":"My mother (A) don't (B) like (C) spicy (D) food.","o":["don't","like","spicy","food"],"k":0,"e":"My mother = she → doesn't.","h":""},{"n":42,"s":"(A) Right now my (B) brothers (C) play video (D) games in their room.","o":["Right now","brothers","play","games"],"k":2,"e":"Right now → present continuous: are playing.","h":""},{"n":43,"s":"(A) My birthday is (B) in the (C) 12th of (D) April.","o":["My","in","12th","April"],"k":1,"e":"Dates take on.","h":""},{"n":44,"s":"I (A) enjoy (B) very much (C) reading (D) books about space.","o":["enjoy","very much","reading","books"],"k":1,"e":"very much goes after the object.","h":""},{"n":45,"s":"Our (A) teacher (B) is (C) usually (D) arrive at seven.","o":["teacher","is","usually","arrive"],"k":3,"e":"The present simple does not use is with a main verb: usually arrives.","h":""},{"n":46,"s":"The (A) students are (B) wearing (C) a new (D) uniforms this year.","o":["students","wearing","a","uniforms"],"k":2,"e":"uniforms is plural, so it cannot follow a.","h":""},{"n":47,"s":"My brother (A) likes tea, (B) so he (C) doesn't like (D) coffee.","o":["likes","so","doesn't","coffee"],"k":1,"e":"Liking tea and not liking coffee is a contrast → but.","h":""},{"n":48,"s":"(A) It is (B) raining (C) hard, so (D) don't forgetting your umbrella.","o":["It","raining","hard","don't forgetting"],"k":3,"e":"After don't we use the base form forget.","h":""},{"n":49,"s":"(A) Because my phone was (B) broken, I (C) couldn't call you (D) in last night.","o":["Because","broken","couldn't","in"],"k":3,"e":"last night needs no preposition.","h":""},{"n":50,"s":"The (A) weather is nice, (B) but my sister (C) is wanting to (D) stay at home.","o":["weather","but","is wanting","stay"],"k":2,"e":"want is stative → wants.","h":""}]}],"n":50}};
